window.__F=window.__F||{};window.__F["acc-13.html"]="<div class=\"ac-info\"><p class=\"ac-i-main\">تشخيص شبكة CAN: حالات عدم استجابة CAN C، وعدم اتصال السكانر مع الشبكتين CAN C وCAN IHS، وجداول الفولتية الطبيعية للأسلاك.</p><p class=\"ac-i-tip\"><b>متى تستعمله:</b> ابدأ من فحص وصلة التشخيص DLC والموصلات النجمية Star Connectors، ثم افصل العقول واحداً بعد الآخر لتعرف أيها يعطّل الشبكة.</p></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">CAN C BUS NO RESPONSE</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">For a complete wiring diagram, refer to appropriate SYSTEM WIRING DIAGRAMS article .</p></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The primary communication network between electronic control modules is the Controller Area Network (CAN) data bus system. The Controller Area Network (CAN) data bus allows all electronic modules connected to the bus to share information with each other. Regardless of whether a message originates from a module on the higher speed CAN C (500K) Bus or on the lower speed bus, CAN Interior High Speed (IHS) (125K) Bus, the message structure and layout is similar, which allows the Body Control Module/Central GateWay (BCM or BCMCGW) to process and transfer messages between the CAN buses. The BCM stores Diagnostic Trouble Codes (DTCs) for certain bus network faults on the CAN C (500K) Bus and CAN IHS (125K) Bus.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">When an open circuit or terminal push out occurs one or more modules can become isolated from the remainder of the bus. The isolated module will attempt to communicate, but will not be able to receive messages or determine arbitration from other modules. Each time the isolated module attempts to communicate it alters the bus voltage on the intact bus circuit. Without functioning arbitration the isolated module alters the bus voltage while other bus messages are being sent thereby corrupting the messages on the remainder of the bus.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The CAN bus modules are connected in parallel to the two-wire bus using a twisted pair, where the wires are wrapped around each other to provide shielding from unwanted electromagnetic induction, thus preventing interference with the relatively low voltage signals being carried through them. While the CAN bus is operating (active), one of the bus wires will carry a higher voltage and is referred to as the CAN bus (+) wire, while the other bus wire will carry a lower voltage and is referred to as the CAN bus (-) wire.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">For additional information on the communication network and star connector locations. Refer to COMMUNICATION, DESCRIPTION .</p><pre class=\"en-pre\">                                CAN Bus Voltages (Normal Operation)\n  CAN-C                                         CAN (-) CAN (+) CAN (-)                CAN (+) CAN (+)\n                        Recessive Dominant\n    Bus        Sleep                            Short to Short to Short to             Short to Short to\n                        (Bus Idle) (Bus Active)\n  Circuits                                      Ground Ground Battery                  Battery CAN (-)\n                                                                                        Battery\n                                                                            Battery     Voltage\n  CAN (-)      0.0 V    2.4 - 2.5 V   1.3 - 2.3 V    0.0 V     0.3 - 0.5V                        2.45 V\n                                                                            Voltage    Less 0.75\n                                                                                          V\n                                                                          Battery\n                                                                          Voltage  Battery\n  CAN (+)      0.0 V    2.4 - 2.5 V   2.6 - 3.5 V    0.02 V      0.0 V                      2.45 V\n                                                                         Less 0.75 Voltage\n                                                                            V\n CAN-IHS                                            CAN (-)     CAN (+) CAN (-) CAN (+) CAN (+)\n    Bus                Sleep          Bus Active    Short to    Short to Short to Short to Short to\n  Circuits                                          Ground      Ground Battery Battery CAN (-)</pre><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">CAN Bus Voltages (Normal Operation) CAN-C                                        CAN (-) CAN (+) CAN (-)                CAN (+) CAN (+) Recessive Dominant Bus       Sleep                            Short to Short to Short to             Short to Short to (Bus Idle) (Bus Active) Circuits                                     Ground Ground Battery                  Battery CAN (-) Battery Battery      Voltage CAN (-)             0.0 V       1.3 - 2.3 V     0.0 V     0.3 - 0.5 V                         2.45 V Voltage     Less 0.75 V Battery Voltage    Battery CAN (+)             0.0 V       2.6 - 3.5 V     0.02 V      0.0 V                             2.45 V Less 0.75   Voltage V Notes All measurements Total resistance of CAN networks can be measured taken between node DVOM will display           with the battery disconnected. The average resistance is ground and CAN average network voltage.    approximately 60.0 Ohms. The termination resistors are terminal with a integral to the Star Connectors. standard DVOM.</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">POSSIBLE CAUSES</strong><small>الأسباب المحتملة</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Possible Causes CAN C BUS (+) CIRCUIT SHORTED TO GROUND</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">ANY MODULE CONNECTED TO THE CAN C BUS</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK THE CAN BUS (-) CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO VOLTAGE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the scan tool.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Measure the voltage between ground and the CAN C Bus (-) circuit.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Is the voltage above 10.0 volts?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Diagnose the short to voltage in the CAN C Bus (-) circuit. Use the Star Connectors to isolate portions of the bus to assist in determining the location of the concern. Repair the circuit concern or replace the module that when disconnected allowed the bus voltage to return to normal.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE CAN C BUS (+) CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO GROUND</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the voltage between ground and the CAN C Bus (+) circuit.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Is the voltage approximately 0 volt?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Diagnose the short to ground in the CAN C Bus (+) circuit. Use the Star Connectors to isolate portions of the bus to assist in determining the location of the concern. Repair the circuit concern or replace the module that when disconnected allowed the bus voltage to return to normal.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK FOR CORRECT BUS TERMINATION RESISTANCE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect and isolate the negative battery cable.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the resistance between the CAN C Bus (+) circuit and the CAN C Bus (-) circuit.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance between 53.5 and 67 Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test complete, the condition or conditions that originally caused this concern are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check the Star Connectors and all related splices for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">For a resistance measurement above 67 Ohms, an open or high resistance is present in the CAN C Bus (+) circuit or the CAN C Bus (-) circuit between the Star Connectors or one of the termination resistors internal to the Star Connector is damaged. Diagnose and repair as necessary. For a resistance measurement below 53.5 Ohms, a short between the CAN C Bus (+) circuit and the CAN C Bus (-) is present. Diagnose the short between the CAN C Bus (+) circuit and the CAN C Bus (-) circuit. Use the Star Connectors to isolate portions of the bus to assist in determining the location of the concern. Repair the circuit concern or replace the module that when disconnected allowed the resistance to return to normal.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">SCAN TOOL DOES NOT COMMUNICATE WITH CAN C AND CAN IHS</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Below are few different ways communication on a vehicle takes place:</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Scan tool to the BCM Module</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Module to Module</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Module to Device</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Device to Module</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Communication to the vehicle is established with a scan tool, through the Data Link Connector (DLC) to the Central GateWay Module (CGW) over the Controller Area Network (CAN) Bus. On this vehicle the Body Control Module (BCM) is the CGW between the high and low speed CAN Bus networks (CAN-C and CAN- IHS); and communicates with the scan tool through CAN C.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The CAN Bus architecture of this vehicle operates in a &quot;hub&quot; or &quot;star&quot; style, meaning all of the modules are connected at a central point in the Star Connectors. The terminating resistors for CAN Bus are located in the Star Connectors that are part of the body and instrument panel wiring harnesses. In other CAN Bus architectures a vehicle may operate in a &quot;stub&quot; or &quot;backbone&quot; style, meaning there is a single, main line that connects all modules. The terminating resistors for CAN Bus in the &quot;stub&quot; or &quot;backbone&quot; style are located in 2 separate dominant modules; that are placed as far apart as is physically possible. The header of the scan tool is populated by the BCM with vehicle data, when communication with the scan tool has been established. The scan tool becomes another module on the vehicle&#x27;s networks by acting as the Master Module of all Bus networks while connected to the DLC; and contributes voltage to the operation of the CAN Bus.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The following vehicle interactions listed below will aid in predetermining the type of vehicle communication that is/isn&#x27;t available:</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           If the Hazard Lamps and Headlamps are active, this indicates the BCM is functioning and is most likely not the cause of the CAN Bus fault.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Operating the Lock/Unlock button of the FOB with Integrated Key (FOBIK) = When any one of the Remote Keyless Entry (RKE) transmitter buttons of the FOBIK are depressed, the on-board transmitter generates a high frequency RF request signal that is received and validated by the Radio Frequency Hub (RF Hub) Module. If the RF Hub determines the RKE transmitter RF request signal was generated by a FOBIK that is valid for the vehicle, the RF Hub relays electronic request messages to the BCM over the CAN Bus to invoke the functions or features associated with the request. Opening a Door = The Door Latches contain Ajar Switches that are hardwired to the BCM. The status of the Door Ajar Switch Sense circuit input is monitored by the BCM, which then sends the proper electronic message to other modules in the vehicle over the CAN Bus. Turning the Headlights on = The Headlamp switch uses a single resistor multiplexed output to control the many functions and features it provides. The switch receives a clean ground from the BCM on a Headlamp Switch MUltipleX (MUX) Return circuit. The BCM then reads the switch outputs using an internal pull up on the Headlamp/Fog Lamp Switch Signal circuit to control the exterior lighting functions Turning the Hazard Lamps on = The status of the Hazard Switch is continually monitored by the circuitry within the Instrument Panel Switch Bank in the Integrated Center Stack (ICS). The switch receives battery voltage at all times through a Fused Battery Feed circuit, and a path to ground at all times through the Instrument Panel wire harness. Whenever the Hazard Switch is in its latched and lowered position, the hazard warning system is selected and the switch bank circuitry provides a hardwired output to the BCM. When the BCM receives a Hazard Switch input, it then controls hazard warning system operation and</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">flash rate by controlling battery voltage outputs through high side drivers on the Right and Left, Front and Rear Turn Signal Feed circuits. Honking the Horn = Each Horn has a path to ground at all times through its wire harness connection to an eyelet terminal secured to the body sheet metal. The Horns are controlled by a Fused B(+) output received through a relay within the front Power Distribution Center (PDC) Assembly and controlled by the BCM.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">During an ignition cycle, the CAN C Bus network may go into default mode when communication has been hindered with the BCM. In some situations, when this happens the Wipers automatically operate in a delay mode and the Headlamps are activated by the BCM. When the ignition is turned off, the vehicle will exit the default mode and operation of the Wipers and Headlamps will stop. When turning the ignition on again, if the CAN C Bus fault is still present, the vehicle will exhibit a no crank, no start condition; and no scan tool communication response to the vehicle. It is important to note the difference between wi-TECH and wi-TECH 2 when diagnosing these type of concerns. The difference between them is, wi-TECH 2 has a faster refresh rate and is capable of communicating with modules over the CAN IHS Bus even when the CAN C Bus has issues with communication.</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic will not have Diagnostic Trouble Codes (DTCs) to assist in determining no scan tool communication with the vehicle.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Default Actions:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Vehicle may start and run. The Wipers and Headlamps may be automatically activated during an ignition cycle when communication is in default mode.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Possible Causes INOPERATIVE SCAN TOOL</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">16</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">ANY MODULE ON THE CAN C BUS</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><pre class=\"en-pre\">NORMAL CAN C BUS CIRCUIT VOLTAGE TABLE\n                   CIRCUIT                           NORMAL VOLTAGE VALUES\nCAN C BUS (-)                              1.5 - 2.5 volts\nCAN C BUS (+)                              2.5 - 3.5 volts\nDifference Between CAN C BUS (+) and CAN C\n                                           0.5 volt\nBUS (-)</pre></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK SCAN TOOL COMMUNICATION</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Verify the scan tool can communicate with another vehicle.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the scan tool communicate with another vehicle?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Contact the scan tool support.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE SCAN TOOL CONNECTION</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Verify all terminals in the DLC are locked into place and there is no damage to the connector or terminals.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are all terminals in the DLC locked into place and no damage found to the connector or terminals?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the DLC and terminals as needed. Once the repair is complete, check the communication between the scan tool and this vehicle.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE DLC (B+) CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Connect a battery charger to the vehicle in accordance with Service Information to maintain a full state of charge throughout testing on this vehicle.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Connect the (special tool #CH7002, Break Out Box, J1962, 16-Way) to the DLC.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Do not connect the scan tool to the Break Out Box.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With a 12-volt test light connected to ground, check the DLC Fused (B+) circuit at the Break Out Box.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The test light must illuminate brightly. Compare the brightness to that of a direct connection to the battery.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the DLC Fused (B+) circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE DLC GROUND CIRCUITS FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With a 12-volt test light connected to 12 volts, check the DLC Ground circuits at the Breakout Box.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The test light must illuminate brightly. Compare the brightness to that of a direct connection to the battery.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 5</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair the DLC Ground circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>DETERMINE THE STATUS OF THE VEHICLE</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Make sure all programmed keys for this specific vehicle are present during the following test steps.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the headlights on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Attempt to start the engine.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:            This step is checking for communication from module to module that may still be possible, even though communication between the vehicle and the scan tool is not.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the engine start or attempt to start by cranking?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 6</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 7</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>VERIFY CAN C BUS VOLTAGE AT THE DLC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the engine off (if the engine started) and turn the ignition to the run position.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:            The vehicle has an operational CAN C bus because the engine was able to crank or start.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:            Do not connect the scan tool to the Break Out Box.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Measure the voltage on the CAN C Bus (+) circuit at the Breakout Box and note the results. Compare the results to the NORMAL CAN CIRCUIT VOLTAGE TABLE.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the voltage on the CAN C Bus (-) circuit at the Breakout Box and note the results. Compare the results to the NORMAL CAN CIRCUIT VOLTAGE TABLE.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are the CAN C circuit voltages within the specified values?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Contact scan tool support.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, continue to diagnosis and test the CAN C Bus circuits and connections from the DLC to the Star Connector for an open or high resistance. Check all related CAN C bus wiring from the DLC to the Star Connector for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension and repair as necessary.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>CHECK THE CAN C BUS VOLTAGES AT THE DATA LINK CONNECTOR</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Connect the (special tool #CH7002, Break Out Box, J1962, 16-Way) to the DLC.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          Do not connect the scan tool to the Break Out Box.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Measure the voltage on the CAN C Bus (+) circuit at the Breakout Box and note the results. Compare the results to the NORMAL CAN CIRCUIT VOLTAGE TABLE.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the voltage on the CAN C Bus (-) circuit at the Breakout Box and note the results. Compare the results to the NORMAL CAN CIRCUIT VOLTAGE TABLE.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Determine which best describes the results found:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">NORMAL - CAN C (+) and (-) voltages</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 8</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">ABNORMAL - CAN C (+) and (-) voltages</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 12</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>CHECK THE CAN C BUS VOLTAGES AT THE REAR/BODY STAR CONNECTOR</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          Depending on the vehicle, either Front and Rear CAN C Star Connectors or IP and Body CAN C Star Connectors will be used.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the 3 wire harness connector at the Rear/Body CAN C Star Connector and check the CAN C bus (+) and (-) voltages between ground and each circuit at the harness connector. Compare the results to the NORMAL CAN CIRCUIT VOLTAGE TABLE.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are the CAN C Bus voltages within the specified values?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 9</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the CAN C bus circuit(s) between the Front/IP and Rear/Body CAN C Star Connectors for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>CHECK THE CAN C BUS VOLTAGES AT THE BODY CONTROL MODULE (BCM)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Connect the 3 wire harness connector to the Rear/Body CAN C Star Connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Connect the scan tool to the (special tool #CH7002, Break Out Box, J1962, 16-Way).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect the BCM connector containing the CAN C circuits.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Check the CAN C bus (+) and (-) voltages between ground and each circuit at the BCM connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Compare the results to the NORMAL CAN CIRCUIT VOLTAGE TABLE.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are the CAN C Bus voltages within the specified values?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 10</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Repair the CAN C bus circuit(s) between the Rear/Body Star Connector and the BCM for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>CHECK ALL FUSED B(+) CIRCUITS TO THE BCM</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the scan tool from the Break Out Box.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect the BCM harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>With a 12-volt test light connected to ground, check the Fused B(+) circuits at the BCM harness connector(s).</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:            The test light must illuminate brightly. Compare the brightness to that of a direct connection to the battery.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly on all power circuit feeds to the BCM?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 11</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Repair the Fused B (+) circuit(s) for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">11</span><span>CHECK ALL GROUND CIRCUITS TO THE BCM</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With a 12-volt test light connected to 12 volts, check all Ground circuits at the BCM connector(s).</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:            The test light must illuminate brightly. Compare the brightness to that of a direct connection to the battery.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly on all ground circuits?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go to 19</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the Ground circuit(s) for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">12</span><span>CHECK THE CAN C BUS VOLTAGES AT THE DLC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          Depending on the vehicle, either Front and Rear CAN C Star Connectors or IP and Body CAN C Star Connectors will be used.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the 3 wire harness connector at the Rear/Body CAN C Star Connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Check the CAN C bus (+) and (-) voltages between ground and each circuit at the DLC. Compare the results to the NORMAL CAN CIRCUIT VOLTAGE TABLE.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are the CAN C Bus voltages within the specified values?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 13</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 15</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">13</span><span>CHECK THE CAN C BUS CIRCUITS TO THE MODULE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Connect the 3 wire harness connector to the Rear/Body CAN C Star Connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect one 2 wire connector from the Rear/Body CAN C Star Connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the voltage on the CAN C (+) circuit at the DLC breakout box. Compare the results to the NORMAL CAN CIRCUIT VOLTAGE TABLE.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Measure the voltage on the CAN C (-) circuit at the DLC breakout box. Compare the results to the NORMAL CAN CIRCUIT VOLTAGE TABLE.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           If the voltage for each CAN C circuit does not read within the specified CAN C circuit voltage range, connect the 2 wire connector back to the Rear/Body CAN C Star Connector and disconnect a different one. Then, repeat the voltage measurements. Repeat as necessary until the CAN C circuit voltages read within the specified CAN C circuit voltage range.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the CAN C voltages read within the specified CAN C circuit voltage range when one of the 2 wire connectors were disconnected?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 14</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Replace the Rear/Body CAN C Star Connector in accordance with Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">14</span><span>CHECK THE MODULE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Connect the 2 wire connector that allowed the CAN C Bus voltages to return to the normal operating range.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the associated module while monitoring the CAN C bus voltages at the DLC. Compare the results to the NORMAL CAN CIRCUIT VOLTAGE TABLE.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the CAN C Bus voltages return to normal operating range?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Replace the associated module in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Repair the CAN C Bus circuits between the Rear/Body Star Connector and the associated module for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">15</span><span>CHECK THE CAN C BUS VOLTAGES</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the 3 wire connector at the Front/IP CAN C Star Connector and check the CAN C bus (+) and (-) voltages at the DLC with the Breakout Box. Compare the results to the NORMAL CAN CIRCUIT VOLTAGE TABLE.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the CAN C Bus voltages return to normal operating range?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Repair the CAN C bus circuits between the Front/IP and Rear/Body CAN C Star Connectors for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 16</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">16</span><span>CHECK THE CAN C BUS CIRCUITS TO THE MODULES</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Connect the 3 wire connectors to the Rear/Body CAN C Star Connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Connect the 3 wire connectors to the Front/IP CAN C Star Connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect one 2 wire connector from the Front/IP CAN C Star Connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Measure the voltage on the CAN C (+) circuit at the DLC breakout box. Compare the results to the NORMAL CAN CIRCUIT VOLTAGE TABLE.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Measure the voltage on the CAN C (-) circuit at the DLC breakout box. Compare the results to the NORMAL CAN CIRCUIT VOLTAGE TABLE.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           If the voltage for each CAN C circuit does not read within the specified CAN C circuit voltage range, connect the 2 wire connector back to the Front/IP CAN C Star Connector and disconnect a different one. Then, repeat the voltage measurements. Repeat as necessary until the CAN C circuit voltages read within the specified CAN C circuit voltage range.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the CAN C Bus voltages return to normal operating range?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 17</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 18</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">17</span><span>CHECK THE MODULE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Connect the 2 wire connector that allowed the CAN C Bus voltages to return to the normal operating range.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the associated module while monitoring the CAN C bus voltages at the DLC. Compare the results to the NORMAL CAN CIRCUIT VOLTAGE TABLE.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the CAN C Bus voltages return to the normal operating range?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Replace the associated module in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Repair the CAN C Bus circuits between the Front/IP CAN C Star Connector and the associated module for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">18</span><span>CHECK THE CAN C BUS CIRCUITS FOR AN OPEN OR SHORT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check the CAN C bus (+) and (-) circuits for continuity to ground, short to voltage and opens from the DLC to the Front/IP CAN C Star Connector. Compare the results to the NORMAL CAN CIRCUIT VOLTAGE TABLE.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the CAN C bus wiring open or shorted?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Repair the CAN C bus circuits between the DLC and the Front/IP Star Connectors for a short to ground, short to voltage or an open.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Replace the Front/IP CAN C Star Connector in accordance with Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">19</span><span>CHECK RELATED HARNESS CONNECTIONS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect all BCM harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect all related in-line harness connections (if equipped).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect the related component harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Inspect harness connectors, component connectors, and all male and female terminals for the following conditions: Proper connector installation. Damaged connector locks. Corrosion. Other signs of water intrusion. Weather seal damage (if equipped).</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Bent terminals. Overheating due to a poor connection (terminal may be discolored due to excessive current draw). Terminals that have been pushed back into the connector cavity.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform a terminal drag test on each connector terminal to verify proper terminal tension.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair any conditions that are found.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Reconnect all BCM harness connectors. Be certain that all harness connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Reconnect all in-line harness connectors (if equipped). Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Reconnect all related component harness connectors. Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Using the recorded Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>With the scan tool, read BCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Body Control Module (BCM) in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, BODY CONTROL (BCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST . Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">17</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">SCAN TOOL DOES NOT COMMUNICATE WITH CAN C</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Below are few different ways communication on a vehicle takes place:</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Scan tool to the BCM Module</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Module to Module</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Module to Device</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Device to Module</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Communication to the vehicle is established with a scan tool, through the Data Link Connector (DLC) to the Central GateWay Module (CGW) over the Controller Area Network (CAN) Bus. On this vehicle the Body Control Module (BCM) is the CGW between the high and low speed CAN Bus networks (CAN-C and CAN- IHS); and communicates with the scan tool through CAN C.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The CAN Bus architecture of this vehicle operates in a &quot;hub&quot; or &quot;star&quot; style, meaning all of the modules are connected at a central point in the Star Connectors. The terminating resistors for CAN Bus are located in the Star Connectors that are part of the body and instrument panel wiring harnesses. In other CAN Bus architectures a vehicle may operate in a &quot;stub&quot; or &quot;backbone&quot; style, meaning there is a single, main line that connects all modules. The terminating resistors for CAN Bus in the &quot;stub&quot; or &quot;backbone&quot; style are located in 2 separate dominant modules; that are placed as far apart as is physically possible. The header of the scan tool is populated by the BCM with vehicle data, when communication with the scan tool has been established. The scan tool becomes another module on the vehicle&#x27;s networks by acting as the Master Module of all Bus networks while connected to the DLC; and contributes voltage to the operation of the CAN Bus.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The following vehicle interactions listed below will aid in predetermining the type of vehicle communication that is/isn&#x27;t available:</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:        If the Hazard Lamps and Headlamps are active, this indicates the BCM is functioning and is most likely not the cause of the CAN Bus fault.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Operating the Lock/Unlock button of the FOB with Integrated Key (FOBIK) = When any one of the Remote Keyless Entry (RKE) transmitter buttons of the FOBIK are depressed, the on-board transmitter generates a high frequency RF request signal that is received and validated by the Radio Frequency Hub (RF Hub) Module. If the RF Hub determines the RKE transmitter RF request signal was generated by a FOBIK that is valid for the vehicle, the RF Hub relays electronic request messages to the BCM over the CAN Bus to invoke the functions or features associated with the request. Opening a Door = The Door Latches contain Ajar Switches that are hardwired to the BCM. The status of the Door Ajar Switch Sense circuit input is monitored by the BCM, which then sends the proper electronic message to other modules in the vehicle over the CAN Bus. Turning the Headlights on = The Headlamp switch uses a single resistor multiplexed output to control the many functions and features it provides. The switch receives a clean ground from the BCM on a Headlamp Switch MUltipleX (MUX) Return circuit. The BCM then reads the switch outputs using an internal pull up on the Headlamp/Fog Lamp Switch Signal circuit to control the exterior lighting functions Turning the Hazard Lamps on = The status of the Hazard Switch is continually monitored by the circuitry within the Instrument Panel Switch Bank in the Integrated Center Stack (ICS). The switch receives battery voltage at all times through a Fused Battery Feed circuit, and a path to ground at all times through the Instrument Panel wire harness. Whenever the Hazard Switch is in its latched and lowered position, the hazard warning system is selected and the switch bank circuitry provides a hardwired output to the BCM. When the BCM receives a Hazard Switch input, it then controls hazard warning system operation and flash rate by controlling battery voltage outputs through high side drivers on the Right and Left, Front and Rear Turn Signal Feed circuits. Honking the Horn = Each Horn has a path to ground at all times through its wire harness connection to an eyelet terminal secured to the body sheet metal. The Horns are controlled by a Fused B(+) output received through a relay within the front Power Distribution Center (PDC) Assembly and controlled by the BCM.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">During an ignition cycle, the CAN C Bus network may go into default mode when communication has been hindered with the BCM. In some situations, when this happens the Wipers automatically operate in a delay mode and the Headlamps are activated by the BCM. When the ignition is turned off, the vehicle will exit the default mode and operation of the Wipers and Headlamps will stop. When turning the ignition on again, if the CAN C Bus fault is still present, the vehicle will exhibit a no crank, no start condition; and no scan tool communication response to the vehicle. It is important to note the difference between wi-TECH and wi-TECH 2 when diagnosing these type of concerns. The difference between them is, wi-TECH 2 has a faster refresh rate and is capable of communicating with modules over the CAN IHS Bus even when the CAN C Bus has issues with communication.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">18</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">POSSIBLE CAUSES - SCAN TOOL DOES NOT COMMUNICATE WITH CAN C (HUB BUS STYLE)</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic will not have Diagnostic Trouble Codes (DTCs) to assist in determining no scan tool communication with the vehicle.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Default Actions:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Vehicle may start and run. The Wipers and Headlamps may be automatically activated during an ignition cycle when communication is in default mode.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Possible Causes INOPERATIVE SCAN TOOL</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">26</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">ANY MODULE ON THE CAN C BUS</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><pre class=\"en-pre\">NORMAL CAN C BUS CIRCUIT VOLTAGE TABLE\n                   CIRCUIT                           NORMAL VOLTAGE VALUES\nCAN C BUS (-)                              1.5 - 2.5 volts\nCAN C BUS (+)                              2.5 - 3.5 volts\nDifference Between CAN C BUS (+) and CAN C\n                                           0.5 volt\nBUS (-)</pre></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK SCAN TOOL COMMUNICATION</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Verify the scan tool can communicate with another vehicle.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the scan tool communicate with another vehicle?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Contact the scan tool support.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE SCAN TOOL CONNECTION</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Verify all terminals in the DLC are locked into place and there is no damage to the connector or terminals.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are all terminals in the DLC locked into place and no damage found to the connector or terminals?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the DLC and terminals as needed. Once the repair is complete, check the communication between the scan tool and this vehicle.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE DLC (B+) CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Connect a battery charger to the vehicle in accordance with Service Information to maintain a full state of charge throughout testing on this vehicle.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Connect the (special tool #CH7002, Break Out Box, J1962, 16-Way) to the DLC.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Do not connect the scan tool to the Break Out Box.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With a 12-volt test light connected to ground, check the DLC Fused (B+) circuit at the Break Out Box.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The test light must illuminate brightly. Compare the brightness to that of a direct connection to the battery.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the DLC Fused (B+) circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE DLC GROUND CIRCUITS FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With a 12-volt test light connected to 12 volts, check the DLC Ground circuits at the Breakout Box.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The test light must illuminate brightly. Compare the brightness to that of a direct connection to the battery.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 5</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair the DLC Ground circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>DETERMINE THE STATUS OF THE VEHICLE</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Make sure all programmed keys for this specific vehicle are present during the following test steps.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the headlights on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Attempt to start the engine.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:            This step is checking for communication from module to module that may still be possible, even though communication between the vehicle and the scan tool is not.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the engine start or attempt to start by cranking?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 6</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 7</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>VERIFY CAN C BUS VOLTAGE AT THE DLC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the engine off (if the engine started) and turn the ignition to the run position.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:            The vehicle has an operational CAN C bus because the engine was able to crank or start.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:            Do not connect the scan tool to the Break Out Box.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Measure the voltage on the CAN C Bus (+) circuit at the Breakout Box and note the results. Compare the results to the NORMAL CAN CIRCUIT VOLTAGE TABLE.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the voltage on the CAN C Bus (-) circuit at the Breakout Box and note the results. Compare the results to the NORMAL CAN CIRCUIT VOLTAGE TABLE.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are the CAN C circuit voltages within the specified values?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Contact scan tool support.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, continue to diagnosis and test the CAN C Bus circuits and connections from the DLC to the Star Connector for an open or high resistance. Check all related CAN C bus wiring from the DLC to the Star Connector for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension and repair as necessary.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>CHECK THE CAN C BUS VOLTAGES AT THE DATA LINK CONNECTOR</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Connect the (special tool #CH7002, Break Out Box, J1962, 16-Way) to the DLC.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:            Do not connect the scan tool to the Break Out Box.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Measure the voltage on the CAN C Bus (+) circuit at the Breakout Box and note the results. Compare the results to the NORMAL CAN CIRCUIT VOLTAGE TABLE.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the voltage on the CAN C Bus (-) circuit at the Breakout Box and note the results. Compare the results to the NORMAL CAN CIRCUIT VOLTAGE TABLE.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Determine which best describes the results found:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">NORMAL - CAN C (+) and (-) voltages</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 8</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">ABNORMAL - CAN C (+) and (-) voltages</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 12</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>CHECK THE CAN C BUS VOLTAGES AT THE REAR/BODY STAR CONNECTOR</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          Depending on the vehicle, either Front and Rear CAN C Star Connectors or IP and Body CAN C Star Connectors will be used.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the 3 wire harness connector at the Rear/Body CAN C Star Connector and check the CAN C bus (+) and (-) voltages between ground and each circuit at the harness connector. Compare the results to the NORMAL CAN CIRCUIT VOLTAGE TABLE.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are the CAN C Bus voltages within the specified values?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 9</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the CAN C bus circuit(s) between the Front/IP and Rear/Body CAN C Star Connectors for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>CHECK THE CAN C BUS VOLTAGES AT THE BODY CONTROL MODULE (BCM)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Connect the 3 wire harness connector to the Rear/Body CAN C Star Connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Connect the scan tool to the (special tool #CH7002, Break Out Box, J1962, 16-Way).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect the BCM connector containing the CAN C circuits.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Check the CAN C bus (+) and (-) voltages between ground and each circuit at the BCM connector. Compare the results to the NORMAL CAN CIRCUIT VOLTAGE TABLE.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are the CAN C Bus voltages within the specified values?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 10</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the CAN C bus circuit(s) between the Rear/Body Star Connector and the BCM for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>CHECK ALL FUSED B(+) CIRCUITS TO THE BCM</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the scan tool from the Break Out Box.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect the BCM harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>With a 12-volt test light connected to ground, check the Fused B(+) circuits at the BCM harness connector(s).</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:            The test light must illuminate brightly. Compare the brightness to that of a direct connection to the battery.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly on all power circuit feeds to the BCM?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 11</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the Fused B (+) circuit(s) for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">11</span><span>CHECK ALL GROUND CIRCUITS TO THE BCM</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With a 12-volt test light connected to 12 volts, check all Ground circuits at the BCM connector(s).</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:            The test light must illuminate brightly. Compare the brightness to that of a direct connection to the battery.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly on all ground circuits?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go to 19</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the Ground circuit(s) for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">12</span><span>CHECK THE CAN C BUS VOLTAGES AT THE DLC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Depending on the vehicle, either Front and Rear CAN C Star Connectors or IP and Body CAN C Star Connectors will be used.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the 3 wire harness connector at the Rear/Body CAN C Star Connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Check the CAN C bus (+) and (-) voltages between ground and each circuit at the DLC. Compare the results to the NORMAL CAN CIRCUIT VOLTAGE TABLE.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are the CAN C Bus voltages within the specified values?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 13</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 15</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">13</span><span>CHECK THE CAN C BUS CIRCUITS TO THE MODULE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Connect the 3 wire harness connector to the Rear/Body CAN C Star Connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect one 2 wire connector from the Rear/Body CAN C Star Connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the voltage on the CAN C (+) circuit at the DLC breakout box. Compare the results to the NORMAL CAN CIRCUIT VOLTAGE TABLE.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Measure the voltage on the CAN C (-) circuit at the DLC breakout box. Compare the results to the NORMAL CAN CIRCUIT VOLTAGE TABLE.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:            If the voltage for each CAN C circuit does not read within the specified CAN C circuit voltage range, connect the 2 wire connector back to the Rear/Body CAN C Star Connector and disconnect a different one. Then, repeat the voltage measurements. Repeat as necessary until the CAN C circuit voltages read within the specified CAN C circuit voltage range.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the CAN C voltages read within the specified CAN C circuit voltage range when one of the 2 wire connectors were disconnected?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 14</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Replace the Rear/Body CAN C Star Connector in accordance with Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">14</span><span>CHECK THE MODULE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Connect the 2 wire connector that allowed the CAN C Bus voltages to return to the normal operating range.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the associated module while monitoring the CAN C bus voltages at the DLC. Compare the results to the NORMAL CAN CIRCUIT VOLTAGE TABLE.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the CAN C Bus voltages return to normal operating range?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the associated module in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the CAN C Bus circuits between the Rear/Body Star Connector and the associated module for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">15</span><span>CHECK THE CAN C BUS VOLTAGES</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the 3 wire connector at the Front/IP CAN C Star Connector and check the CAN C bus (+) and (-) voltages at the DLC with the Breakout Box. Compare the results to the NORMAL CAN CIRCUIT VOLTAGE TABLE.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the CAN C Bus voltages return to normal operating range?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the CAN C bus circuits between the Front/IP and Rear/Body CAN C Star Connectors for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 16</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">16</span><span>CHECK THE CAN C BUS CIRCUITS TO THE MODULES</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Connect the 3 wire connectors to the Rear/Body CAN C Star Connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Connect the 3 wire connectors to the Front/IP CAN C Star Connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect one 2 wire connector from the Front/IP CAN C Star Connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Measure the voltage on the CAN C (+) circuit at the DLC breakout box. Compare the results to the NORMAL CAN CIRCUIT VOLTAGE TABLE.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Measure the voltage on the CAN C (-) circuit at the DLC breakout box. Compare the results to the NORMAL CAN CIRCUIT VOLTAGE TABLE.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           If the voltage for each CAN C circuit does not read within the specified CAN C circuit voltage range, connect the 2 wire connector back to the Front/IP CAN C Star Connector and disconnect a different one. Then, repeat the voltage measurements. Repeat as necessary until the CAN C circuit voltages read within the specified CAN C circuit voltage range.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the CAN C Bus voltages return to normal operating range?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 17</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 18</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">17</span><span>CHECK THE MODULE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Connect the 2 wire connector that allowed the CAN C Bus voltages to return to the normal operating range.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the associated module while monitoring the CAN C bus voltages at the DLC. Compare the results to the NORMAL CAN CIRCUIT VOLTAGE TABLE.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the CAN C Bus voltages return to the normal operating range?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the associated module in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the CAN C Bus circuits between the Front/IP CAN C Star Connector and the associated module for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">18</span><span>CHECK THE CAN C BUS CIRCUITS FOR AN OPEN OR SHORT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check the CAN C bus (+) and (-) circuits for continuity to ground, short to voltage and opens from the DLC to the Front/IP CAN C Star Connector. Compare the results to the NORMAL CAN CIRCUIT VOLTAGE TABLE.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the CAN C bus wiring open or shorted?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the CAN C bus circuits between the DLC and the Front/IP Star Connectors for a short to ground, short to voltage or an open.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Front/IP CAN C Star Connector in accordance with Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">19</span><span>CHECK RELATED HARNESS CONNECTIONS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect all BCM harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect all related in-line harness connections (if equipped).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect the related component harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Inspect harness connectors, component connectors, and all male and female terminals for the following conditions: Proper connector installation. Damaged connector locks. Corrosion. Other signs of water intrusion. Weather seal damage (if equipped). Bent terminals. Overheating due to a poor connection (terminal may be discolored due to excessive current draw). Terminals that have been pushed back into the connector cavity.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform a terminal drag test on each connector terminal to verify proper terminal tension.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair any conditions that are found.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Reconnect all BCM harness connectors. Be certain that all harness connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Reconnect all in-line harness connectors (if equipped). Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Reconnect all related component harness connectors. Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Using the recorded Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>With the scan tool, read BCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Body Control Module (BCM) in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, BODY CONTROL (BCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST . Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">27</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">SCAN TOOL DOES NOT COMMUNICATE WITH CAN IHS</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Below are few different ways communication on a vehicle takes place:</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Scan tool to the BCM Module</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Module to Module</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Module to Device</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Device to Module</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Communication to the vehicle is established with a scan tool, through the Data Link Connector (DLC) to the Central GateWay Module (CGW) over the Controller Area Network (CAN) Bus. On this vehicle the Body Control Module (BCM) is the CGW between the high and low speed CAN Bus networks (CAN-C and CAN- IHS) and communicates with the scan tool through the CAN C Bus.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The CAN Bus architecture of this vehicle operates in a &quot;hub&quot; or &quot;star&quot; style, meaning all of the modules are connected at a central point in the Star Connectors. The terminating resistors for the CAN Bus are located in the Star Connectors that are part of the Body and Instrument Panel wiring harnesses. In other CAN Bus architectures, a vehicle may operate in a &quot;stub&quot; or &quot;backbone&quot; style, meaning there is a single, main line that connects all modules. The terminating resistors for a CAN Bus in the &quot;stub&quot; or &quot;backbone&quot; style are located in 2 separate dominant modules, that are placed as far apart as is physically possible. The header of the scan tool is populated by the BCM with vehicle data, when communication with the scan tool has been established. The scan tool becomes another module on the vehicle&#x27;s Bus networks by acting as the Master Module of all Bus networks while connected to the DLC, and contributes voltage to the operation of the CAN Bus.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">It is important to note the difference between wi-TECH and wi-TECH 2 when diagnosing these type of concerns. The difference between them is wi-TECH 2 has a faster refresh rate and is capable of communicating with modules over the CAN IHS Bus even when CAN C Bus has issues with communication.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">28</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">POSSIBLE CAUSES - SCAN TOOL DOES NOT COMMUNICATE WITH CAN IHS</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic will not have Diagnostic Trouble Codes (DTCs) to assist in determining no scan tool communication with the vehicle.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Possible Causes Possible Causes INOPERATIVE SCAN TOOL</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">34</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">ANY MODULE ON THE CAN IHS BUS</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><pre class=\"en-pre\">NORMAL CAN IHS BUS CIRCUIT VOLTAGE TABLE\n                   CIRCUIT                           NORMAL VOLTAGE VALUES\nCAN IHS BUS (-)                            1.5 - 2.5 volts\nCAN IHS BUS (+)                            2.5 - 3.5 volts\nDifference Between CAN IHS BUS (+) and CAN\n                                           0.5 volt\nIHS BUS (-)</pre></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK SCAN TOOL COMMUNICATION</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Verify the scan tool can communicate with another vehicle.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the scan tool communicate with another vehicle?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Contact the scan tool support.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE SCAN TOOL CONNECTION</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Verify all terminals in the DLC are locked into place and there is no damage to the connector or terminals.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are all terminals in the DLC locked into place and no damage found to the connector or terminals?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the DLC and terminals as needed. Once the repair is complete, check the communication between the scan tool and this vehicle.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE CAN IHS BUS VOLTAGES AT THE DATA LINK CONNECTOR</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Connect a battery charger to the vehicle in accordance with Service Information to maintain a full state of charge throughout testing on this vehicle.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Turn the ignition to the &quot;ON&quot; position.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Connect the (special tool #CH7002, Break Out Box, J1962, 16-Way) to the DLC.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          Do not connect the scan tool to the Break Out Box.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Measure the voltage on the CAN IHS Bus (+) circuit at the Breakout Box and note the results. Compare the results to the NORMAL CAN CIRCUIT VOLTAGE TABLE.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Measure the voltage on the CAN IHS Bus (-) circuit at the Breakout Box and note the results. Compare the results to the NORMAL CAN CIRCUIT VOLTAGE TABLE.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Determine which best describes the results found:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">NORMAL - CAN IHS (+) and (-) voltages</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">For a Dual Star Connector CAN IHS system = Go To 4 For a Single Star Connector CAN IHS system = Go To 15</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">ABNORMAL - CAN IHS (+) and (-) voltages</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">For a Dual Star Connector CAN IHS system = Go To 8 For a Single Star Connector CAN IHS system = Go To 18</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE CAN IHS BUS VOLTAGES AT THE REAR/BODY STAR CONNECTOR (DUAL STAR CONNECTOR SYSTEM)</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          Depending on the vehicle, either Front and Rear CAN IHS Star Connectors or IP and Body CAN IHS Star Connectors will be used.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the 3 wire harness connector at the Rear/Body CAN IHS Star Connector and check the CAN IHS bus (+) and (-) voltages between ground and each circuit at the harness connector. Compare the results to the NORMAL CAN CIRCUIT VOLTAGE TABLE.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Are the CAN IHS Bus voltages within the specified values?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 5</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the CAN IHS bus circuit(s) between the Front/IP and Rear/Body CAN IHS Star Connectors for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>CHECK THE CAN IHS BUS VOLTAGES AT THE BODY CONTROL MODULE (BCM) (DUAL STAR CONNECTOR SYSTEM)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Connect the 3 wire harness connector to the Rear/Body CAN IHS Star Connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the BCM connector containing the CAN IHS circuits.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Check the CAN IHS bus (+) and (-) voltages between ground and each circuit at the BCM connector. Compare the results to the NORMAL CAN CIRCUIT VOLTAGE TABLE.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Are the CAN IHS Bus voltages within the specified values?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 6</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the CAN IHS bus circuit(s) between the Rear/Body Star Connector and the BCM for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>CHECK ALL FUSED B(+) CIRCUITS TO THE BCM (DUAL STAR CONNECTOR SYSTEM)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the BCM harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With a 12-volt test light connected to ground, check the Fused B(+) circuits at the BCM harness connector(s).</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The test light must illuminate brightly. Compare the brightness to that of a direct connection to the battery.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly on all power circuit feeds to the BCM?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 7</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the Fused B (+) circuit(s) for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>CHECK ALL GROUND CIRCUITS TO THE BCM (DUAL STAR CONNECTOR SYSTEM)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With a 12-volt test light connected to 12 volts, check all Ground circuits at the BCM connector(s)</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The test light must illuminate brightly. Compare the brightness to that of a direct connection to the battery.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly on all ground circuits?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go to 21</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the Ground circuit(s) for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>CHECK THE CAN IHS BUS VOLTAGES AT THE DLC (DUAL STAR CONNECTOR SYSTEM)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the 3 wire harness connector at the Rear/Body CAN IHS Star Connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Check the CAN IHS bus (+) and (-) voltages between ground and each circuit at the DLC. Compare the results to the NORMAL CAN CIRCUIT VOLTAGE TABLE.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are the CAN IHS Bus voltages within the specified values?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 9</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 11</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>CHECK THE CAN IHS BUS CIRCUITS TO THE MODULE (DUAL STAR CONNECTOR SYSTEM)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Connect the 3 wire harness connector to the Rear/Body CAN IHS Star Connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect one 2 wire connector from the Rear Rear/Body IHS Star Connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the voltage on the CAN C (+) circuit at the DLC breakout box. Compare the results to the NORMAL CAN CIRCUIT VOLTAGE TABLE.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Measure the voltage on the CAN C (-) circuit at the DLC breakout box. Compare the results to the NORMAL CAN CIRCUIT VOLTAGE TABLE.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           If the voltage for each CAN C circuit does not read within the specified CAN C circuit voltage range, connect the 2 wire connector back to the Rear/Body CAN IHS Star Connector and disconnect a different one. Then, repeat the voltage measurements. Repeat as necessary until the CAN C circuit voltages read within the specified CAN C circuit voltage range.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the CAN C voltages read within the specified CAN C circuit voltage range when one of the 2 wire connectors were disconnected?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 10</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Rear/Body CAN IHS Star Connector in accordance with Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>CHECK THE MODULE (DUAL STAR CONNECTOR SYSTEM)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Connect the 2 wire connector that allowed the CAN IHS Bus voltages to return to the normal operating range.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the associated module while monitoring the CAN IHS bus voltages at the DLC. Compare the results to the NORMAL CAN CIRCUIT VOLTAGE TABLE.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the CAN IHS Bus voltages return to normal operating range?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the associated module in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the CAN IHS Bus circuits between the Rear/Body Star Connector and the associated</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">module for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">11</span><span>CHECK THE CAN IHS BUS VOLTAGES (DUAL STAR CONNECTOR SYSTEM)</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          Depending on the vehicle, either Front and Rear CAN IHS Star Connectors or IP and Body CAN IHS Star Connectors will be used.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the 3 wire connector at the Front/IP CAN IHS Star Connector and check the CAN IHS bus (+) and (-) voltages at the DLC with the Breakout Box. Compare the results to the NORMAL CAN CIRCUIT VOLTAGE TABLE.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the CAN IHS Bus voltages return to normal operating range?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the CAN C bus circuits between the Front/IP and Rear/Body CAN IHS Star Connectors for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 12</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">12</span><span>CHECK THE CAN IHS BUS CIRCUITS TO THE MODULES (DUAL STAR CONNECTOR SYSTEM)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Connect the 3 wire connectors to the Rear/Body CAN IHS Star Connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Connect the 3 wire connectors to the Front/IP CAN IHS Star Connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect one 2 wire connector from the Front/IP CAN IHS Star Connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Measure the voltage on the CAN IHS (+) circuit at the DLC breakout box. Compare the results to the NORMAL CAN CIRCUIT VOLTAGE TABLE.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Measure the voltage on the CAN IHS (-) circuit at the DLC breakout box. Compare the results to the NORMAL CAN CIRCUIT VOLTAGE TABLE.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           If the voltage for each CAN IHS circuit does not read within the specified CAN IHS circuit voltage range, connect the 2 wire connector back to the Front/IP CAN IHS Star Connector and disconnect a different one. Then, repeat the voltage measurements. Repeat as necessary until the CAN IHS circuit voltages read within the specified CAN IHS circuit voltage range.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the CAN IHS Bus voltages return to normal operating range?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 13</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 14</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">13</span><span>CHECK THE MODULE (DUAL STAR CONNECTOR SYSTEM)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Connect the 2 wire connector that allowed the CAN IHS Bus voltages to return to the normal operating range.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the associated module while monitoring the CAN IHS bus voltages at the DLC. Compare the results to the NORMAL CAN CIRCUIT VOLTAGE TABLE.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the CAN IHS Bus voltages return to the normal operating range?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the associated module in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the CAN IHS Bus circuits between the Front/IP CAN IHS Star Connector and the associated module for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">14</span><span>CHECK THE CAN IHS BUS CIRCUITS FOR AN OPEN OR SHORT (DUAL STAR CONNECTOR SYSTEM)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check the CAN IHS bus (+) and (-) circuits for continuity to ground, short to voltage and opens from the DLC to the Front/IP CAN IHS Star Connector. Compare the results to the NORMAL CAN CIRCUIT VOLTAGE TABLE.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the CAN IHS bus wiring open or shorted?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the CAN IHS bus circuits between the DLC and the Front/IP Star Connectors for a short to ground, short to voltage or an open.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Front/IP CAN IHS Star Connector in accordance with Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">15</span><span>CHECK THE CAN IHS BUS VOLTAGES AT THE BODY CONTROL MODULE (BCM) (SINGLE STAR CONNECTOR SYSTEM)</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Depending on the vehicle, either Front and Rear CAN IHS Star Connectors or IP and Body CAN IHS Star Connectors will be used.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the BCM connector containing the CAN IHS circuits.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Check the CAN IHS bus (+) and (-) voltages between ground and each circuit at the BCM connector. Compare the results to the NORMAL CAN CIRCUIT VOLTAGE TABLE.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are the CAN IHS Bus voltages within the specified values?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 16</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the CAN IHS bus circuit(s) between the Rear/Body Star Connector and the BCM for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">16</span><span>CHECK ALL FUSED B(+) CIRCUITS TO THE BCM (SINGLE STAR CONNECTOR SYSTEM)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the BCM harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With a 12-volt test light connected to ground, check the Fused B(+) circuits at the BCM harness connector(s).</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:            The test light must illuminate brightly. Compare the brightness to that of a direct connection to the battery.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly on all power circuit feeds to the BCM?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 17</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the Fused B (+) circuit(s) for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">17</span><span>CHECK ALL GROUND CIRCUITS TO THE BCM (SINGLE STAR CONNECTOR SYSTEM)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With a 12-volt test light connected to 12 volts, check all Ground circuits at the BCM connector(s).</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:            The test light must illuminate brightly. Compare the brightness to that of a direct connection to the battery.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly on all ground circuits?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go to 21</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the Ground circuit(s) for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">18</span><span>CHECK THE CAN IHS BUS VOLTAGES (SINGLE STAR CONNECTOR SYSTEM)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect one 2 wire connector from the CAN IHS Star Connector going to a module, leaving the BCM last.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Measure the voltage on the CAN IHS (+) circuit at the DLC breakout box. Compare the results to the NORMAL CAN CIRCUIT VOLTAGE TABLE.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the voltage on the CAN IHS (-) circuit at the DLC breakout box. Compare the results to the NORMAL CAN CIRCUIT VOLTAGE TABLE.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           If the voltage for each CAN IHS circuit does not read within the specified CAN IHS circuit voltage range, connect the 2 wire connector back to the CAN IHS Star Connector and disconnect a different one, leaving the BCM last. Then, repeat the voltage measurements. Repeat as necessary until the CAN IHS circuit voltages read within the specified CAN IHS circuit voltage range.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the CAN IHS Bus voltages return to normal operating range?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 19</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 20</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">19</span><span>CHECK THE MODULE</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Depending on the vehicle, either Front and Rear CAN IHS Star Connectors or IP and Body CAN IHS Star Connectors will be used.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Connect the 2 wire connector that allowed the CAN IHS Bus voltages to return to the normal operating range.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the associated module while monitoring the CAN IHS bus voltages at the DLC. Compare the results to the NORMAL CAN CIRCUIT VOLTAGE TABLE.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the CAN IHS Bus voltages return to the normal operating range?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the associated module in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the CAN IHS Bus circuits between the Front/IP CAN IHS Star Connector and the associated module for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">20</span><span>CHECK THE CAN IHS BUS CIRCUITS FROM THE DLC TO THE STAR CONNECTOR</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check the CAN IHS bus (+) and (-) circuits for continuity to ground, short to voltage and opens from the DLC to the CAN IHS Star Connector. Compare the results to the NORMAL CAN CIRCUIT VOLTAGE TABLE.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the CAN IHS bus wiring open or shorted?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the CAN IHS bus circuits between the DLC and the Star Connector for a short to ground, short to voltage or an open.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the CAN IHS Star Connector in accordance with Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">21</span><span>CHECK RELATED HARNESS CONNECTIONS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect all BCM harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect all related in-line harness connections (if equipped).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect the related component harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Inspect harness connectors, component connectors, and all male and female terminals for the following conditions: Proper connector installation. Damaged connector locks. Corrosion. Other signs of water intrusion. Weather seal damage (if equipped). Bent terminals. Overheating due to a poor connection (terminal may be discolored due to excessive current draw). Terminals that have been pushed back into the connector cavity.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform a terminal drag test on each connector terminal to verify proper terminal tension.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair any conditions that are found.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Reconnect all BCM harness connectors. Be certain that all harness connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Reconnect all in-line harness connectors (if equipped). Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Reconnect all related component harness connectors. Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Using the recorded Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>With the scan tool, read BCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Replace the Body Control Module (BCM) in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, BODY CONTROL (BCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST . Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">35</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">NO RESPONSE FROM ABS (ANTI-LOCK BRAKE SYSTEM) MODULE</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">POSSIBLE CAUSES</strong><small>الأسباب المحتملة</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Possible Causes FUSED B(+) CIRCUITS OPEN OR SHORTED</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Possible Causes FUSED RUN/START RELAY OUTPUT CIRCUIT OPEN OR SHORTED</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">39</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">ANTI-LOCK BRAKE SYSTEM (ABS) MODULE</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>TEST FOR INTERMITTENT CONDITION</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Check for any Service Bulletins related to the condition. If a Service Bulletin applies, perform the procedure outlined in the Service Bulletin before continuing with this procedure.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Make sure the battery voltage is between 10.0 and 16.0 volts.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read the module status.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Check the BCM for any active CAN DTCs and perform the appropriate diagnostics before proceeding. Refer to DIAGNOSTIC CODE INDEX .</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Does the scan tool indicate that the module is active on the bus?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the Stored Lost Communication DTCs diagnostic procedure. Refer to DIAGNOSIS AND TESTING.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK (A107) AND (A200) FUSED B(+) CIRCUITS FOR AN OPEN OR SHORT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Anti-lock Brake System (ABS) Module harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The test light must illuminate brightly. Compare the brightness to that of a direct connection to the battery.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Using a 12-volt test light connected to ground, check the (A107) and the (A200) Fused B(+) circuits at the ABS Module harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly for each circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the Fused B(+) circuits for an open or short.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ABS VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ABS VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (F941) IGNITION RUN/START CONTROL OUTPUT CIRCUIT FOR OPEN OR SHORT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using a 12-volt test light connected to ground, check the (F941) Ignition Run/Start Control Output circuit at the ABS Module harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (F941) Ignition Run/Start Control Output circuit for an open or short.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ABS VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ABS VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (Z802) GROUND CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Using a 12-volt test light connected to 12-volts, check the (Z802) Ground circuit at the ABS Module harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 5</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (Z802) Ground circuit for an open.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ABS VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ABS VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>CHECK THE (D497) CAN C (+) BUS CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Star CAN C Front C8 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (D497) CAN C (+) bus circuit between the Star CAN C Front C8 harness connector and the ABS Module harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is resistance below 3.0 Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 6</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair the (D497) CAN C (+) bus circuit for an open.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the ABS VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ABS VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>CHECK THE (D498) CAN C (-) BUS CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (D498) CAN C (-) bus circuit between the Star CAN C Front C8 harness connector and the ABS Module harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Is resistance below 3.0 Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Replace the Anti-lock Brake System (ABS) Module in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, ANTI-LOCK BRAKE SYSTEM (ABS), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the ABS VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ABS VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair the (D498) CAN C (-) bus circuit for an open.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the ABS VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ABS VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">40</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">NO RESPONSE FROM ACC (ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL) MODULE</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">POSSIBLE CAUSES</strong><small>الأسباب المحتملة</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Possible Causes FUSED IGNITION CIRCUIT OPEN OR SHORTED GROUND CIRCUIT OPEN OR HIGH RESISTANCE Possible Causes CAN C BUS (+) CIRCUIT OPEN OR HIGH RESISTANCE</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">42</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) MODULE</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK IF THE MODULE IS ACTIVE ON THE BUS</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Check for any Service Bulletins (SB) related to the condition and perform the procedure outlined in the SB before continuing.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Make sure the battery voltage is between 10.0 and 16.0 volts.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read the Module status.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Check the BCM for any active CAN hardware DTCs and perform DTC diagnostics before proceeding.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the scan tool indicate that the Module is active on the bus?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The no response condition is not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE (F948) FUSED IGNITION CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN OR SHORT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) Module harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>With a 12-volt test light connected to ground, check the (F948) Fused Ignition circuit at the ACC Module harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The test light must illuminate brightly. Compare the brightness to that of a direct connection to the battery.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (F948) Fused Ignition circuit for an open.</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           If the fuse is open, make sure to check for a short to ground.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (Z902) GROUND CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With a 12-volt test light connected to 12 volts, check the (Z902) Ground circuit at the ACC Module harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (Z902) Ground circuit for an open.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (D249) AND (D248) CAN C BUS CIRCUITS FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the CAN C Star Connector Front C12 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (D249) CAN C Bus (+) circuit between the CAN C Star Connector Front C12 harness connector and the ACC Module harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (D248) CAN C Bus (-) circuit between the CAN C Star Connector Front C12 harness connector and the ACC Module harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 3.0 Ohms on each circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) Module in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (D249) or (D248) CAN C Bus circuit(s) for an open.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">43</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">NO RESPONSE FROM ADCM (ACTIVE DAMPING CONTROL MODULE)</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">POSSIBLE CAUSES</strong><small>الأسباب المحتملة</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Possible Causes FUSED RUN RELAY OUTPUT CIRCUITS OPEN OR SHORTED</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">47</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">ACTIVE DAMPING CONTROL MODULE (ADCM)</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>TEST FOR INTERMITTENT CONDITION</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          Check for any Service Bulletins related to the condition. If a Service Bulletin applies, perform the procedure outlined in the Service Bulletin before continuing with this procedure.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Make sure the battery voltage is between 10.0 and 16.0 volts.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read the module status.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Check the BCM for any active CAN hardware DTCs, perform DTC before proceeding.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the scan tool indicate that the module is active on the bus?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The no response condition is not present at this time. Using the wiring diagram/schematic as a guide, inspect the wiring for chafed, pierced, pinched, and partially broken wires and the wiring harness connectors for broken, bent, pushed out, and corroded terminals.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE (F930) FUSED RUN RELAY OUTPUT CIRCUITS FOR AN OPEN OR SHORT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Active Damping Control Module (ADCM) C1 and C2 harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The test light must illuminate brightly. Compare the brightness to that of a direct connection to the battery.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using a 12-volt test light connected to ground, check each (F930) Fused Run Relay Output circuits at the ADCM C2 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly for each circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the open or short in the (F930) Fused Run Relay Output circuits.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (Z922) GROUND CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using a 12-volt test light connected to 12-volts, check the (Z922) Ground circuit at the ADCM C2 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the open in the (Z922) Ground circuit.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (D152) CAN C (-) BUS CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Star CAN C Rear C8 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (D152) CAN C (-) bus circuit between the Star CAN C Rear C8 harness connector and the ADCM C1 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 3.0 Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 5</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the open in the (D152) CAN C (-) bus circuit. Inspect the connector for damage.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>CHECK THE (D153) CAN C (+) BUS CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (D153) CAN C (+) bus circuit between the CAN C Star Rear C8 harness connector and the ADCM C1 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 3.0 Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Active Damping Control Module (ADCM) in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, ACTIVE DAMPING CONTROL (ADCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the open in the (D153) CAN C (+) bus circuit. Inspect the connector for damage.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">48</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">NO RESPONSE FROM AMP (AMPLIFIER)</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">POSSIBLE CAUSES</strong><small>الأسباب المحتملة</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Possible Causes FUSED B (+) CIRCUIT OPEN OR SHORTED</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">51</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">CAN IHS BUS (-) CIRCUIT OPEN</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Possible Causes AMPLIFIER</p></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>TEST FOR AN INTERMITTENT CONDITION</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:         Check for any TSB(s) related to the condition. If a TSB applies, perform the procedure outlined in the TSB before continuing.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:         Make sure the battery voltage is between 10.0 and 16.0 volts.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:         Check the Amplifier (AMP) for any active CAN hardware DTCs, perform DTC before proceeding.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read the AMP status.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Does the scan tool indicate the AMP is active on the bus?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The no response condition is not present at this time. Using the wiring diagram/schematic as a guide, inspect the wiring for chafed, pierced, pinched, and partially broken wires and the wiring harness connectors for broken, bent, pushed out, and corroded terminals.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE (A931) FUSED B(+) CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN OR SHORT CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:         The test light must illuminate brightly. Compare the brightness to that of a direct connection to the battery.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the AMP C1 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Using a 12-volt test light connected to ground, check the (A931) Fused B(+) circuit at the AMP C1 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the open or short in the (A931) Fused B(+) circuit.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (Z911) GROUND CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Using a 12-volt test light connected to 12-volts, check the (Z911) Ground circuits at the AMP C1 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the open in the (Z911) Ground circuit.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (D207) CAN IHS BUS (+) AND (D206) CAN IHS BUS (-) CIRCUITS FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Front CAN IHS Star Connector C7 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (D207) CAN C Bus (+) circuit between the Front CAN IHS Star Connector C7 harness connector and the AMP C1 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (D206) CAN C Bus (-) circuit between the Front CAN IHS Star Connector C7 harness connector and the AMP C1 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance above 3.0 Ohms for both circuits?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the open in the (D207) CAN IHS Bus (+) or (D206) CAN IHS Bus (-) circuit.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Amplifier (AMP) in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to AMPLIFIER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">52</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">NO RESPONSE FROM BCM (BODY CONTROL MODULE)</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">POSSIBLE CAUSES</strong><small>الأسباب المحتملة</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Possible Causes FUSED B(+) CIRCUIT(S) OPEN OR SHORTED</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">56</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">BODY CONTROL MODULE (BCM)</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>TEST FOR AN INTERMITTENT CONDITION</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:       If the scan tool is unable to identify the vehicle, a CAN C bus concern may be present. and perform the CAN C BUS NO RESPONSE diagnostic procedure. Refer to DIAGNOSIS AND TESTING.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:       Check for any TSB(s) related to the condition. If a TSB applies, perform the procedure outlined in the TSB before continuing.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:       Make sure the battery voltage is between 10.0 and 16.0 volts.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          Check the Body Control Module (BCM) for any active CAN hardware DTCs, perform DTC before proceeding.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read the BCM status.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the scan tool indicate the BCM is active on the bus?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The no response condition is not present at this time. Using the wiring diagram/schematic as a guide, inspect the wiring for chafed, pierced, pinched, and partially broken wires and the wiring harness connectors for broken, bent, pushed out, and corroded terminals.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE (A903) AND (A904) FUSED B(+) CIRCUITS FOR AN OPEN OR SHORT CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the BCM C2/B and C3/C harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The test light must illuminate brightly. Compare the brightness to that of a direct connection to the battery.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Using a 12-volt test light connected to ground, check the (A903) and (A904) Fused B(+) circuits at the BCM C2/B and C3/C harness connectors.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly for each circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the open or short in the (A903) or (A904) Fused B(+) circuit.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE GROUND CIRCUITS FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Using a 12-volt test light connected to 12-volts, check the Ground circuits at the BCM C2/B and C3/C harness connectors.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly for each circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the open in the Ground circuit.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (D45) CAN C BUS (+) AND (D46) CAN C BUS (-) CIRCUITS FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the BCM C5/E harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Rear CAN C Star Connector C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (D45) CAN C Bus (+) circuit between the Rear CAN C Star Connector C2 harness connector and the BCM C5/E harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (D46) CAN C Bus (-) circuit between the Rear CAN C Star Connector C2 harness connector and the BCM C5/E harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Is the resistance above 3.0 Ohms for both circuits?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the open in the (D45) CAN C Bus (+) or (D46) CAN C Bus (-) circuit.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Body Control Module (BCM) in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, BODY CONTROL (BCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">57</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">NO RESPONSE FROM DDM (DRIVER DOOR MODULE)</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">POSSIBLE CAUSES</strong><small>الأسباب المحتملة</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Possible Causes FUSED B (+) CIRCUIT OPEN OR SHORTED</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">61</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DRIVER DOOR MODULE (DDM)</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK THE DRIVER DOOR MODULE STATUS ON THE CAN IHS BUS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read the module status.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the scan tool indicate that the module is active on the bus?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The no response condition is not present at this time. Using the wiring diagram/schematic as a guide, inspect the wiring for chafed, pierced, pinched, and partially broken wires and the wiring harness connectors for broken, bent, pushed out, and corroded terminals.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE (A924) FUSED B(+) CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN OR SHORT TO GROUND</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Leave the scan tool</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">connected</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">and on the initial network screen.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Driver Door Module C3 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With a 12-volt test light connected to ground, check the (A924) Fused B(+) circuit at the Driver Door Module C3 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The test light must illuminate brightly. Compare the brightness to that of a direct connection to the battery.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (A924) Fused B(+) circuit for an open or short to ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (Z916) GROUND CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN OR HIGH RESISTANCE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With a 12-volt test light connected to 12 volts, check the (Z916) Ground circuit at the Driver Door Module C3 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (Z916) ground circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE CAN IHS BUS (+) CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN OR HIGH RESISTANCE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the voltage between ground and the (D103) CAN IHS Bus (+) circuit at the Driver Door Module C3 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the voltage below 2.5 volts?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (D103) CAN IHS Bus (+) circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 5</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>CHECK THE CAN IHS BUS (-) CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN OR HIGH RESISTANCE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the voltage between ground and the (D104) CAN IHS Bus (-) circuit at the Driver Door Module C3 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the voltage below 1.3 volts?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (D104) CAN IHS Bus (-) circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Driver Door Module in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, DOOR (DDM/PDM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">62</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">NO RESPONSE FROM DTCM (DRIVETRAIN CONTROL MODULE)</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">POSSIBLE CAUSES</strong><small>الأسباب المحتملة</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Possible Causes FUSED B(+) CIRCUIT OPEN OR SHORTED</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">67</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DRIVE TRAIN CONTROL MODULE (DTCM)</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          Check for any TSB(s) related to the condition. If a TSB applies, perform the procedure outlined in the TSB before continuing.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Make sure the battery voltage is between 10.0 and 16.0 volts.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read the Module status.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Check the BCM for any active CAN DTCs and perform the appropriate diagnostics before proceeding. Refer to DIAGNOSTIC CODE INDEX .</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the scan tool indicate that the Module is active on the bus?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the Stored Lost Communication DTCs diagnostic procedure. Refer to DIAGNOSIS AND TESTING.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE (A194) FUSED B(+) CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN OR SHORT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the DTCM C1 and C2 harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>With a 12-volt test light connected to ground, check the (A194) Fused B(+) circuit.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (A194) Fused B(+) circuit for an open or short.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the DTCM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to DTCM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (F946) FUSED IGNITION SWITCH OUTPUT (RUN-START) CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN OR SHORT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With a 12-volt test light connected to ground, check the (F946) Fused Ignition Switch Output (Run- Start) circuit.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (F946) Fused Ignition Switch Output (Run-Start) circuit for an open or short.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the DTCM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to DTCM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (Z924) GROUND CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN OR HIGH RESISTANCE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With a 12-volt test light connected to 12 volts, check the (Z924) Ground circuit.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 5</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (Z924) Ground circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the DTCM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to DTCM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>CHECK THE (D301) CAN C(+) BUS CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN OR HIGH RESISTANCE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the Star Can C Body C11 harness connector. and perform the CAN C DASH STAR CONNECTOR REMOVAL process. Refer to STANDARD PROCEDURE .</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (D301) CAN C Bus (+) circuit between the Star Can C Body C11 harness connector and the DTCM C1 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistances below 3.0 Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 6</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (D301) CAN C(+) Bus circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the DTCM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to DTCM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>CHECK THE (D302) CAN C(-) BUS CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN OR HIGH RESISTANCE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (D302) CAN C Bus (-) circuit between the Star Can C Body C11 harness connector and the DTCM C1 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are the resistances below 3.0 Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Drive Train Control Module (DTCM) in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, DRIVETRAIN CONTROL (DTCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the DTCM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to DTCM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (D302) CAN C(-) Bus circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the DTCM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to DTCM VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">68</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">NO RESPONSE FROM EPS (ELECTRIC POWER STEERING) MODULE</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">POSSIBLE CAUSES</strong><small>الأسباب المحتملة</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Possible Causes FUSED B(+) CIRCUIT OPEN OR SHORTED</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">73</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">ELECTRIC POWER STEERING (EPS) MODULE</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>TEST FOR INTERMITTENT CONDITION</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:       Check for any Service Bulletins related to the condition. If a Service</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Bulletin applies, perform the procedure outlined in the Service Bulletin before continuing with this procedure.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Make sure the battery voltage is between 10.0 and 16.0 volts.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read the module status.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Check the BCM for any active CAN hardware DTCs, perform the diagnostic procedure for those DTCs before proceeding.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the scan tool indicate that the module is active on the bus?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The no response condition is not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE (A951) FUSED B(+) CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN OR SHORT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Electric Power Steering (EPS) Module C1 and C2 harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The test light must illuminate brightly. Compare the brightness to that of a direct connection to the battery.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using a 12-volt test light connected to ground, check the (A951) Fused B(+) circuit at the EPS C1 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (A951) Fused B(+) circuit for an open or short.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the EPS VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to EPS VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (F944) FUSED IGNITION SWITCH OUTPUT (RUN-START) CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN OR SHORT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Using a 12-volt test light connected to ground, check the (F944) Fused Ignition Switch Output (Run-Start) circuit at the EPS C2 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (F944) Fused Ignition Switch Output (Run-Start) circuit for an open or short.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the EPS VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to EPS VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (Z906) GROUND CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using a 12-volt test light connected to 12-volts, check the (Z906) Ground circuit at the EPS C1 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 5</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (Z906) Ground circuit for an open.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the EPS VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to EPS VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>CHECK THE (D139) CAN C (+) BUS CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the Star CAN C Front C9 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (D139) CAN C (+) bus circuit between the Star CAN C Front C9 harness connector and the EPS C2 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistances below 3.0 Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 6</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (D139) CAN C (+) bus circuit for an open.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the EPS VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to EPS VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>CHECK THE (D138) CAN C (-) BUS CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (D138) CAN C (-) bus circuit between the Star CAN C Front C9 harness connector and the EPS C2 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are the resistances below 3.0 Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Electric Power Steering (EPS) Module in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to GEAR, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the EPS VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to EPS VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair the (D138) CAN C (-) bus circuit for an open.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the EPS VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to EPS VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">74</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">NO RESPONSE FROM ESM (ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE) - NAG1</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">POSSIBLE CAUSES</strong><small>الأسباب المحتملة</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Possible Causes (F1) FUSED IGNITION SWITCH OUTPUT (OFF-RUN-START) CIRCUIT OPEN OR SHORTED (Z916) GROUND CIRCUIT OPEN (D64) OR (D65) CAN C BUS CIRCUITS OPEN ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM)</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Always perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding. Refer to COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK THE MODULE STATUS ON THE CONTROLLER AREA NETWORK (CAN) C BUS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read the CAN topology on the Vehicle View screen.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Does the Vehicle View screen indicate that the Module is active on the bus?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct terminal tension and repair as necessary. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the Electronic Shift Module (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST. For 8HP45/845RE,</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Refer to ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST . For 8HP70,</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Refer to ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST . For 8HP90,</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Refer to ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE (F1) IGNITION OFF/RUN/START CONTROL OUTPUT CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN OR SHORT TO GROUND</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:         The CAN bus will remain active with the scan tool connected and the ignition off.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:         Leave the scan tool connected</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">and on the Vehicle View screen.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the ESM harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>With a 12-volt test light connected to ground, check the (F1) Ignition Off/Run/Start Control Output circuit at the ESM harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The test light must illuminate brightly. Compare the brightness to that of a direct connection to the battery.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (F1) Ignition Off/Run/Start Control Output circuit for an open or short to ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ESM VERIFICATION TEST. For 8HP45/845RE, Refer to ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST . For 8HP70, Refer to ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST . For 8HP90, Refer to ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (Z916) GROUND CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN OR HIGH RESISTANCE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With a 12-volt test light connected to 12 volts, check the (Z916) Ground circuit at the ESM harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (Z916) Ground circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ESM VERIFICATION TEST. For 8HP45/845RE, Refer to ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST . For 8HP70, Refer to ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST . For 8HP90, Refer to ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (D65) CAN C BUS (+) CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN OR HIGH RESISTANCE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the voltage on the (D65) CAN C Bus (+) circuit at the ESM harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the voltage below 2.5 volts?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (D65) CAN C Bus (+) circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ESM VERIFICATION TEST. For 8HP45/845RE, Refer to ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST . For 8HP70, Refer to ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST . For 8HP90, Refer to ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 5</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>CHECK THE (D64) CAN C BUS (-) CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN OR HIGH RESISTANCE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the voltage on the (D64) CAN C Bus (-) circuit at the ESM harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the voltage below 1.3 volts?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (D64) CAN C Bus (-) circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ESM VERIFICATION TEST. For 8HP45/845RE, Refer to ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST . For 8HP70, Refer to ELECTRONIC</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST . For 8HP90, Refer to ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Replace the ESM in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, ELECTRONIC SHIFT (ESM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the ESM VERIFICATION TEST. For 8HP45/845RE, Refer to ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST . For 8HP70, Refer to ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST . For 8HP90, Refer to ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">75</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">NO RESPONSE FROM ESM (ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE) 8-SPEED</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">POSSIBLE CAUSES</strong><small>الأسباب المحتملة</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Possible Causes FUSED B (+) CIRCUIT OPEN OR SHORTED</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">79</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM)</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Always perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding. Refer to COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK THE MODULE STATUS ON THE CONTROLLER AREA NETWORK (CAN) C BUS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read the CAN topology on the Vehicle View screen.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Does the Vehicle View screen indicate that the Module is active on the bus?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this Diagnostic Trouble Code (DTC) are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct terminal tension and repair as necessary. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ESM VERIFICATION TEST. For 8HP45/845RE, Refer to ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST . For 8HP70, Refer to ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST . For 8HP90, Refer to ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE (A190) FUSED B(+) CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN OR SHORT TO GROUND</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:         The CAN bus will remain active with the scan tool connected and the ignition off.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:         Leave the scan tool connected</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">and on the Vehicle View screen.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Electronic Shift Module (ESM) harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With a 12-volt test light connected to ground, check the (A190) Fused B(+) circuit at the ESM harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The test light must illuminate brightly. Compare the brightness to that of a direct connection to the battery.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (A190) Fused B(+) circuit for an open or short to ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ESM VERIFICATION TEST. For 8HP45/845RE, Refer to ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST . For 8HP70, Refer to ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST . For 8HP90, Refer to ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (Z911) GROUND CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN OR HIGH RESISTANCE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With a 12-volt test light connected to 12 volts, check the (Z911) Ground circuit at the ESM harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (Z911) Ground circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ESM VERIFICATION TEST. For 8HP45/845RE, Refer to ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST . For 8HP70, Refer to ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST . For 8HP90, Refer to ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (D430) CAN C BUS (+) CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN OR HIGH RESISTANCE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the voltage on the (D430) CAN C Bus (+) circuit at the ESM harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the voltage below 2.5 volts?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (D430) CAN C Bus (+) circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ESM VERIFICATION TEST. For 8HP45/845RE, Refer to ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST . For 8HP70, Refer to ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST . For 8HP90, Refer to ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 5</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>CHECK THE (D429) CAN C BUS (-) CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN OR HIGH RESISTANCE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the voltage on the (D429) CAN C Bus (-) circuit at the ESM harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the voltage below 1.3 volts?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (D429) CAN C Bus (-) circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ESM VERIFICATION TEST. For 8HP45/845RE, Refer to ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST . For 8HP70, Refer to ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST . For 8HP90, Refer to ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Replace the ESM in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the ESM VERIFICATION TEST. For 8HP45/845RE, Refer to ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST . For 8HP70, Refer to ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST . For 8HP90, Refer to ELECTRONIC SHIFT MODULE (ESM) VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">80</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">NO RESPONSE FROM FFCM (FORWARD FACING CAMERA MODULE)</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">POSSIBLE CAUSES</strong><small>الأسباب المحتملة</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Possible Causes FUSED IGNITION CIRCUIT OPEN OR SHORTED</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">84</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">FORWARD FACING CAMERA MODULE (FFCM)</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:       Check for any TSB(s) related to the condition. If a TSB applies, perform the</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">procedure outlined in the TSB before continuing.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Make sure the battery voltage is between 10.0 and 16.0 volts.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read the Module status.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Check the BCM for any active CAN C hardware DTCs and perform the appropriate diagnostic procedure before proceeding.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the scan tool indicate that the Module is active on the bus?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The no response condition is not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE (Z911) GROUND CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Forward Facing Camera Module harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With a 12-volt test light connected to 12-volts, check the (Z911) Ground circuit at the Forward Facing Camera Module harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The test light must illuminate brightly. Compare the brightness to that of a direct connection to the battery.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (Z911) Ground circuit for an open.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the FORWARD FACING CAMERA VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to FORWARD FACING CAMERA VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (F924) FUSED IGNITION CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN OR SHORT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With a 12-volt test light connected to ground, check the (F924) Fused Ignition circuit at the Forward Facing Camera Module harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (F924) Fused Ignition circuit for an open.</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          If the fuse is open, make sure to check the circuit for a short to ground.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the FORWARD FACING CAMERA VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to FORWARD FACING CAMERA VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (D349) AND (D348) CAN C BUS CIRCUITS FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Star CAN C harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (D349) CAN C Bus (+) circuit between the Front Star CAN C harness connector and the Forward Facing Camera Module harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (D348) CAN C Bus (-) circuit between the Front Star CAN C harness connector and the Forward Facing Camera Module harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 3.0 Ohms on both circuits?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Using the schematics as a guide, check the FFCM pins, terminals, and connectors for corrosion, damage, or terminal push out. Pay particular attention to all power and ground circuits. Is no problems are found, replace and program the Forward Facing Camera Module (FFCM) in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, FORWARD FACING CAMERA (FFCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the FORWARD FACING CAMERA VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to FORWARD FACING CAMERA VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (D349) or (D348) CAN C Bus circuit for an open.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the FORWARD FACING CAMERA VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to FORWARD FACING CAMERA VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">85</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">NO RESPONSE FROM HSM (HEATED SEAT MODULE)</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">POSSIBLE CAUSES</strong><small>الأسباب المحتملة</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Possible Causes FUSED IGNITION CIRCUIT OPEN OR SHORTED</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">89</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">HEATED SEAT MODULE (HSM)</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK IF THE MODULE IS ACTIVE ON THE BUS</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          Check for any Service Bulletins (SB) related to the condition. If a SB applies, perform the procedure outlined in the SB before continuing.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          Make sure the battery voltage is between 10.0 and 16.0 volts.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read the Module status.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Check the BCM for any active CAN hardware DTCs and perform DTC</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">diagnostics before proceeding.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the scan tool indicate that the Module is active on the bus?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The no response condition is not present at this time. Using the wiring diagram/schematic as a guide, inspect the wiring for chafed, pierced, pinched, and partially broken wires and the wiring harness connectors for broken, bent, pushed out, and corroded terminals.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE (F921) FUSED IGNITION CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN OR SHORT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Heated Seat Module (HSM) C1 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>With a 12-volt test light connected to ground, check the (F921) Fused Ignition circuit at the HSM C1 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The test light must illuminate brightly. Compare the brightness to that of a direct connection to the battery.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (F921) Fused Ignition circuit for an open.</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           If the fuse is open, make sure to check for a short to ground.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (Z917) GROUND CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With a 12-volt test light connected to 12 volts, check the (Z917) Ground circuit at the HSM C1 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (Z917) Ground circuit for an open.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (D163) AND (D164) CAN IHS BUS (125K) CIRCUITS FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the Rear CAN IHS Star Connector C3 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (D164) CAN IHS Bus (-) circuit between the Rear CAN IHS Star Connector C3 harness connector and the HSM C1 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (D163) CAN IHS Bus (+) circuit between the Rear CAN IHS Star Connector C3 harness connector and the HSM C1 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">IS the resistance below 3.0 Ohms on each circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Heated Seat Module in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, HEATED SEAT (HSM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (D163) or (D164) CAN IHS Bus circuit(s) for an open.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">90</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">NO RESPONSE FROM HVAC</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">POSSIBLE CAUSES</strong><small>الأسباب المحتملة</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Possible Causes FUSED B(+) CIRCUIT OPEN OR SHORTED</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">94</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">HVAC MODULE</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>TEST FOR INTERMITTENT CONDITION</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          Check for any TSB(s) related to the condition. If a TSB applies, perform the procedure outlined in the TSB before continuing.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Make sure the battery voltage is between 10.0 and 16.0 volts.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read the module status.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Check the BCM for any active CAN hardware DTCs, perform DTC before proceeding.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Does the scan tool indicate that the module is active on the bus?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The no response condition is not present at this time. Using the wiring diagram/schematic as a guide, inspect the wiring for chafed, pierced, pinched, and partially broken wires and the wiring harness connectors for broken, bent, pushed out, and corroded terminals.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE (A938) FUSED B(+) CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN OR SHORT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the HVAC Module harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The test light must illuminate brightly. Compare the brightness to that of a direct connection to the battery.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Using a 12-volt test light connected to ground, check the (A938) Fused B(+) circuit in the HVAC Module harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the open or short in the (A938) Fused B(+) circuit.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the HVAC VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to HVAC VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (Z911) GROUND CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Using a 12-volt test light connected to 12-volts, check the (Z911) Ground circuit in the HVAC Module harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the open in the (Z911) Ground circuit.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the HVAC VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to HVAC VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (F925) FUSED IGNITION SWITCH OUTPUT (RUN) CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN OR SHORT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using a 12-volt test light connected to ground, check the (F925) Fused Ignition Switch Output (RUN) circuit in the HVAC Module harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 5</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the open or short in the (F925) Fused Ignition Switch Output (RUN) circuit.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the HVAC VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to HVAC VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>CHECK THE (D101) AND (D102) CAN IHS BUS (125K) CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Front CAN IHS Star Connector C4 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (D102) CAN IHS Bus (-) (125K) circuit between the Front CAN IHS Star Connector C4 harness connector and the HVAC harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (D101) CAN IHS Bus (+) (125K) circuit between the Front CAN IHS Star Connector C4 harness connector and the HVAC harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are the resistances below 3.0 Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the HVAC Module in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, HVAC, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the HVAC VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to HVAC VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair the open in the (D101) or (D102) CAN IHS Bus (125K) circuit. Inspect the connector for damage.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the HVAC VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to HVAC VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">95</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">NO RESPONSE FROM ICS (INTEGRATED CENTER STACK)</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">POSSIBLE CAUSES</strong><small>الأسباب المحتملة</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Possible Causes FUSED B (+) CIRCUIT OPEN OR SHORTED</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">99</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">INTEGRATED CENTER STACK (ICS)</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>TEST FOR AN INTERMITTENT CONDITION</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Check for any TSB(s) related to the condition. If a TSB applies, perform the procedure outlined in the TSB before continuing.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Make sure the battery voltage is between 10.0 and 16.0 volts.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Check the Integrated Center Stack (ICS) for any active CAN hardware DTCs, perform DTC before proceeding.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read the ICS status.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the scan tool indicate the ICS is active on the bus?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The no response condition is not present at this time. Using the wiring diagram/schematic as a guide, inspect the wiring for chafed, pierced, pinched, and partially broken wires and the wiring harness connectors for broken, bent, pushed out, and corroded terminals.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE (A937) FUSED B(+) CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN OR SHORT CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The test light must illuminate brightly. Compare the brightness to that of a direct connection to the battery.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the ICS harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Using a 12-volt test light connected to ground, check the (A937) Fused B(+) circuit at the ICS harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the open or short in the (A937) Fused B(+) circuit.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (Z911) GROUND CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Using a 12-volt test light connected to 12-volts, check the (Z911) Ground circuits at the ICS harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the open in the (Z911) Ground circuit.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (D463) CAN IHS BUS (+) AND (D462) CAN IHS BUS (-) CIRCUITS FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Front CAN IHS Star Connector C8 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (D463) CAN C Bus (+) circuit between the Front CAN IHS Star Connector C8 harness connector and the ICS harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (D462) CAN C Bus (-) circuit between the Front CAN IHS Star Connector C8 harness connector and the ICS harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance above 3.0 Ohms for both circuits?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the open in the (D463) CAN IHS Bus (+) or (D462) CAN IHS Bus (-) circuit.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Integrated Center Stack (ICS) in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to AMPLIFIER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">100</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">NO RESPONSE FROM IPC (INSTRUMENT PANEL CLUSTER)</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">POSSIBLE CAUSES</strong><small>الأسباب المحتملة</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Possible Causes FUSED B(+) CIRCUIT OPEN OR SHORTED</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">105</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">INSTRUMENT PANEL CLUSTER (IPC)</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK IF THE MODULE IS ACTIVE ON THE BUS</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          Check for any Service Bulletins (SB) related to the condition. If a SB applies, perform the procedure outlined in the SB before continuing.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          Make sure the battery voltage is between 10.0 and 16.0 volts.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read the Module status.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Check the BCM for any active CAN hardware DTCs and perform the DTC diagnostics before proceeding.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the scan tool indicate that the Module is active on the bus?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The no response condition is not present at this time. Using the wiring diagram/schematic as a guide, inspect the wiring for chafed, pierced, pinched, and partially broken wires and the wiring harness connectors for broken, bent, pushed out, and corroded terminals.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE (A938) FUSED B(+) CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN OR SHORT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Instrument Panel Cluster (IPC) harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With a 12-volt test light connected to ground, check the (A938) Fused B(+) circuit at the IPC harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The test light must illuminate brightly. Compare the brightness to that of a direct connection to the battery.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (A938) Fused B(+) circuit for an open.</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           If the fuse is open, make sure to check for a short to ground.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (F924) FUSED IGNITION CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN OR SHORT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With a 12-volt test light connected to ground, check the (F924) Fused Ignition circuit at the IPC harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (F924) Fused Ignition circuit for an open.</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:            If the fuse is open, make sure to check for a short to ground.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (Z910) GROUND CIRCUITS FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With a 12-volt test light connected to 12 volts, check each (Z910) Ground circuit at the IPC harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly for each circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 5</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (Z910) Ground circuit(s) for an open.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>CHECK THE (D82) AND (D81) CAN C BUS CIRCUITS FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Front CAN C Star Connector C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (D81) CAN C Bus (+) circuit between the Front CAN C Star Connector C2 harness connector and the Instrument Cluster harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (D82) CAN C Bus (-) circuit between the Front CAN C Star Connector C2 harness connector and the Instrument Cluster harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 3.0 Ohms on each circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Instrument Cluster in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair (D82) or (D81) CAN C Bus circuit(s) for an open.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">106</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">NO RESPONSE FROM LBSS (LEFT BLIND SPOT SENSOR)</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">POSSIBLE CAUSES</strong><small>الأسباب المحتملة</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Possible Causes FUSED B (+) CIRCUIT OPEN OR SHORTED</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">110</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">LEFT BLIND SPOT SENSOR (LBSS)</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>TEST FOR AN INTERMITTENT CONDITION</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:       Check for any TSB(s) related to the condition. If a TSB applies, perform the procedure outlined in the TSB before continuing.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:       Make sure the battery voltage is between 10.0 and 16.0 volts.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:       Check the Left Blind Spot Sensor (LBSS) for any active CAN hardware DTCs, perform DTC before proceeding.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read the LBSS status.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the scan tool indicate the LBSS is active on the bus?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The no response condition is not present at this time. Using the wiring diagram/schematic as a guide, inspect the wiring for chafed, pierced, pinched, and partially broken wires and the wiring harness connectors for broken, bent, pushed out, and corroded terminals.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE (F923) FUSED B(+) CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN OR SHORT CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The test light must illuminate brightly. Compare the brightness to that of a direct connection to the battery.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the LBSS harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Using a 12-volt test light connected to ground, check the (F923) Fused B(+) circuit at the LBSS harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the open or short in the (F923) Fused B(+) circuit.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (Z922) GROUND CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Using a 12-volt test light connected to 12-volts, check the (Z922) Ground circuit at the LBSS harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair the open in the (Z922) Ground circuit.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (D115) CAN IHS BUS (+) AND (D116) CAN IHS BUS (-) CIRCUITS FOR AN</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">OPEN</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Rear CAN IHS Star Connector C4 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (D115) CAN C Bus (+) circuit between the Rear CAN IHS Star Connector C4 harness connector and the LBSS harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (D116) CAN C Bus (-) circuit between the Rear CAN IHS Star Connector C4 harness connector and the LBSS harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Is the resistance above 3.0 Ohms for both circuits?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair the open in the (D115) CAN IHS Bus (+) or (D116) CAN IHS Bus (-) circuit.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Replace the Left Blind Spot Sensor (LBSS) in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Refer to MODULE, BLIND SPOT (BSM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">111</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">NO RESPONSE FROM MSMD (MEMORY SEAT MODULE)</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">POSSIBLE CAUSES</strong><small>الأسباب المحتملة</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Possible Causes FUSED B(+) CIRCUIT OPEN OR SHORTED</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">114</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">CAN IHS BUS (-) CIRCUIT OPEN OR HIGH RESISTANCE</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Possible Causes MEMORY SEAT MODULE-DRIVER (MSMD)</p></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK IF THE MODULE IS ACTIVE ON THE BUS</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Check for any Service Bulletins (SB) related to the condition. If a SB applies, perform the procedure outlined in the SB before continuing.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Make sure the battery voltage is between 10.0 and 16.0 volts.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read the Module status.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Check the BCM for any active CAN hardware DTCs and perform the DTC diagnostics before proceeding.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the scan tool indicate that the Module is active on the bus?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The no response condition is not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE (A942) FUSED B(+) CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Memory Seat Module C1 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With a 12-volt test light connected to ground, check the (A942) Fused B(+) circuit.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The test light must illuminate brightly. Compare the brightness to that of a direct connection to the battery.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (A942) Fused B(+) circuit for an open.</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           If the fuse is open, make sure to check for a short to ground.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (Z916) GROUND CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With a 12-volt test light connected to 12 volts, check the (Z916) Ground circuit.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (Z916) Ground circuit for an open.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (D165/D265) AND (D166/D264) CAN INTERIOR BUS (125K) CIRCUITS FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the Front CAN IHS Star Connector C6 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (D166/D264) CAN IHS (-) circuit between the Front CAN IHS Star Connector C6 harness connector and the Memory Seat Module C1 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (D165/D265) CAN IHS (+) circuit between the Front CAN IHS Star Connector C6 harness connector and the Memory Seat Module C1 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are the resistances below 3.0 Ohms on each circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Memory Seat Module in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, MEMORY, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (D165/D265) or (D166/D264) CAN IHS circuit(s) for an open.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">115</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">NO RESPONSE FROM ORC OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">POSSIBLE CAUSES</strong><small>الأسباب المحتملة</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Possible Causes FUSED IGNITION SWITCH OUTPUT (RUN) CIRCUIT OPEN OR SHORTED</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">119</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER (ORC) MODULE</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:        The use of a approved special tool or Digital Multimeter such as a Fluke Meter that will not apply more than 20 milliamperes to a circuit are the only measurement tools to be used.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:        Probing of the circuit cavities at the ORC Module C1-A, C1-B, or C2-A body harness connectors is only to be done with a approved test lead from the , test lead 10159-6 or the use of Breakout Box 8443-55 to prevent vehicle wiring harness connector damage during diagnostic procedures.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          Check for any TSB(s) related to the condition. If a TSB applies, perform the procedure outlined in the TSB before continuing.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>TEST FOR INTERMITTENT CONDITION</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Make sure the battery voltage is between 10.0 and 16.0 volts.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read the module status.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Check the BCM for any active CAN hardware DTCs, perform DTC before proceeding.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Does the scan tool indicate that the module is active on the bus?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The no response condition is not present at this time. Using the wiring diagram/schematic as a guide, inspect the wiring for chafed, pierced, pinched, and partially broken wires and the wiring harness connectors for broken, bent, pushed out, and corroded terminals.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Go To 1</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE (Z918) GROUND CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:       Turn the ignition off disconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the Occupant Restraint Controller Module harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Check connectors - Clean and repair as necessary.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Connect the test leads to the DVOM.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the resistance between ground and the (Z918) Ground circuit terminal cavity C1 - 20.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Is the resistance below 3.0 Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair the open in the (Z918) Ground circuit.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (F100) FUSED IGNITION SWITCH OUTPUT (RUN) CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">OR SHORT</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Check the BCM for any ignition related DTCs before proceeding. If set.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Refer to DTC INDEX .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the standard key ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Turn the ignition on, then reconnect the 12-volt battery and wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>If the vehicle is equipped with the keyless ignition, follow this ignition on warning.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">WARNING:        Disconnect the 12-volt battery wait two minutes before proceeding, remove the ORC fuses, connect the 12-volt battery, wait two minutes before proceeding. Cycle the ignition to the On position, then reconnect the ORC fuses. Wait two minutes before proceeding. Failure to follow these instructions may result in possible serious or fatal injury.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Using a 12-volt test light connected to ground, check the (F100) Fused Ignition Switch Output (Run) circuit terminal C2 - 104 of the ORC module.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The test light must illuminate brightly. Compare the brightness to that of a direct connection to the battery.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the open or short in the (F100) Fused Ignition Switch Output (Run) circuit.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (F201) IGNITION RUN/START CONTROL OUTPUT CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN OR SHORT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Using a 12-volt test light connected to ground, check the (F201) Ignition Run/Start Control Output circuit terminal C2 - 103 of the ORC module.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The test light must illuminate brightly. Compare the brightness to that of a direct connection to the battery.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the open or short in the (F201) Ignition Run/Start Control Output circuit.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>CHECK THE (D11) AND (D12) CAN C BUS CIRCUITS FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Front CAN C Star Connector C10 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (D11) CAN C Bus (+) circuit between the Front CAN C Star Connector C10-1 harness connector and the ORC module terminal C2 - 54.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (D12) CAN C Bus (-) circuit between the Front CAN C Star Connector C10-2 harness connector and the ORC module terminal C2 - 53.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are the resistances below 3.0 Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Occupant Restraint Controller in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the open in the (D11) CAN C Bus (+) or (D12) CAN C Bus (-) circuit.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to RESTRAINTS SYSTEM VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">120</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">NO RESPONSE FROM PCM (POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE) - GAS</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">For a complete wiring diagram, refer to appropriate SYSTEM WIRING DIAGRAMS article .</p></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">POSSIBLE CAUSES</strong><small>الأسباب المحتملة</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Possible Causes FUSED B(+) CIRCUIT OPEN OR SHORTED</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">125</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM)</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK BATTERY VOLTAGE</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:         Check for any Service Bulletins related to the condition. If a Service Bulletin applies, perform the procedure outlined in the Service Bulletin before continuing.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Check the Battery voltage.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Check the BCM for any active CAN hardware DTCs, perform DTC before proceeding.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Is the Battery voltage between 10.0 and 16.0 volts?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Charge and test the Battery before continuing.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. For 3.6L. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST . For 5.7L, refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST . For 6.2L, refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST . For 6.4L, refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>TEST FOR INTERMITTENT CONDITION</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read the PCM status.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Does the scan tool indicate that the PCM is active on the bus?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The no response condition is not present at this time. Using the wiring diagram/schematic as a guide, inspect the wiring for chafed, pierced, pinched, and partially broken wires and the wiring harness connectors for broken, bent, pushed out, and corroded terminals.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (A209) FUSED B(+) CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN OR SHORT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the PCM C1 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"ct-warn en-kw\">CAUTION:        Do not probe the PCM harness connectors. Probing the PCM harness connectors will damage the PCM terminals resulting in poor terminal to pin connection. Install the GPEC Diagnostic Adaptor to perform the diagnosis.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Connect the (special tool #10436, Adapter, GPEC Diagnostic).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using a 12-volt test light connected to ground, probe the (A209) Fused B(+) circuit at the GPEC Adaptor.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (A209) Fused B(+) circuit for an open or short to ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. For 3.6L. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST . For 5.7L, refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST . For 6.2L, refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST . For 6.4L, refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (Z903) GROUND CIRCUITS FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Connect the 12-volt test light to 12 volts and probe the (Z903) Ground circuits at the GPEC Adaptor.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly for each circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 5</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (Z903) Ground circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. For 3.6L. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST . For 5.7L, refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST . For 6.2L, refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST . For 6.4L, refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>CHECK THE (D27) AND (D28) CAN C BUS CIRCUITS FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the Front CAN C Star Connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (D27) CAN C Bus (+) circuit between the Front CAN C Star Connector and the GPEC Adaptor.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (D28) CAN C Bus (-) circuit between the Front CAN C Star Connector and the GPEC Adaptor.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance of both circuits below 3.0 Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 5</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (D27) or (D28) CAN C Bus circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. For 3.6L. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST . For 5.7L, refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST . For 6.2L, refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST . For 6.4L, refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>CHECK THE (F942) FUSED IGNITION SWITCH OUTPUT (RUN-START) CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN OR SHORT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Reconnect the PCM C1 harness connector with the GPEC Adaptor still connected.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Reconnect the Front CAN C Star Connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using a 12-volt test light connected to ground, probe the (F942) Fused Ignition Switch Output (Run-Start) circuit.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Replace and program the Powertrain Control Module in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, POWERTRAIN CONTROL (PCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. For 3.6L. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST . For 5.7L, refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST . For 6.2L, refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST . For 6.4L, refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair the (F942) Fused Ignition Switch Output (Run-Start) circuit for an open or short to ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST. For 3.6L. Refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST . For 5.7L, refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST . For 6.2L, refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST . For 6.4L, refer to POWERTRAIN VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">126</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">NO RESPONSE FROM PDM (PASSENGER DOOR MODULE)</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">POSSIBLE CAUSES</strong><small>الأسباب المحتملة</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Possible Causes FUSED B (+) CIRCUIT OPEN OR SHORTED</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">130</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">PASSENGER DOOR MODULE (PDM)</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK THE PASSENGER DOOR MODULE STATUS ON THE CAN IHS BUS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read the module status.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the scan tool indicate that the module is active on the bus?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The no response condition is not present at this time. Using the wiring diagram/schematic as a guide, inspect the wiring for chafed, pierced, pinched, and partially broken wires and the wiring harness connectors for broken, bent, pushed out, and corroded terminals.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE (A925) FUSED B(+) CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN OR SHORT TO GROUND</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Leave the scan tool</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">connected</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">and on the initial network screen.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Passenger Door Module C3 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With a 12-volt test light connected to ground, check the (A925) Fused B(+) circuit at the Passenger Door Module C3 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The test light must illuminate brightly. Compare the brightness to that of a direct connection to the battery.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (A925) Fused B(+) circuit for an open or short to ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (Z917) GROUND CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN OR HIGH RESISTANCE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With a 12-volt test light connected to 12 volts, check the (Z917) Ground circuit at the Passenger Door Module C3 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (Z917) Ground circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE CAN IHS BUS (+) CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN OR HIGH RESISTANCE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the voltage between ground and the (D213) CAN IHS Bus (+) circuit at the Passenger Door Module C3 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the voltage below 2.5 volts?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (D213) CAN IHS Bus (+) circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 5</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>CHECK THE CAN IHS BUS (-) CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN OR HIGH RESISTANCE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the voltage between ground and the (D214) CAN IHS Bus (-) circuit at the Passenger Door Module C3 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the voltage below 1.3 volts?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (D214) CAN IHS Bus (-) circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Passenger Door Module in accordance with the service information. Refer to MODULE, DOOR (DDM/PDM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">131</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">NO RESPONSE FROM PTS (PARK ASSIST MODULE)</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">POSSIBLE CAUSES</strong><small>الأسباب المحتملة</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Possible Causes FUSED B(+) CIRCUIT OPEN OR SHORTED</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">135</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">PARK ASSIST MODULE (PAM)</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>TEST FOR AN INTERMITTENT CONDITION</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          If the scan tool is unable to identify the vehicle, a CAN C bus concern may be present. and perform the CAN C BUS NO RESPONSE diagnostic procedure. Refer to DIAGNOSIS AND TESTING.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          Check for any TSB(s) related to the condition. If a TSB applies, perform the procedure outlined in the TSB before continuing.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          Make sure the battery voltage is between 10.0 and 16.0 volts.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          Check the Park Assist Module (PAM) for any active CAN hardware DTCs, perform DTC before proceeding.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read the PAM status.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Does the scan tool indicate the PAM is active on the bus?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The no response condition is not present at this time. Using the wiring diagram/schematic as a guide, inspect the wiring for chafed, pierced, pinched, and partially broken wires and the wiring harness connectors for broken, bent, pushed out, and corroded terminals.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE (F923) FUSED B(+) CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN OR SHORT CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          The test light must illuminate brightly. Compare the brightness to that of a direct connection to the battery.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the PAM C1 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Using a 12-volt test light connected to ground, check the (F923) Fused B(+) circuits at the PAM C1 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair the open or short in the (F923) Fused B(+) circuit.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (Z922) GROUND CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Using a 12-volt test light connected to 12-volts, check the (Z922) Ground circuit at the PAM C1 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the open in the (Z922) Ground circuit.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (D77) CAN C BUS (+) AND (D78) CAN C BUS (-) CIRCUITS FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Rear CAN C Star Connector C6 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (D77) CAN C Bus (+) circuit between the Rear CAN C Star Connector C6 harness connector and the PAM C1 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (D78) CAN C Bus (-) circuit between the Rear CAN C Star Connector C6 harness connector and the PAM C1 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Is the resistance above 3.0 Ohms for both circuits?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the open in the (D77) CAN C Bus (+) or (D78) CAN C Bus (-) circuit.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Park Assist Module (PAM) in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, PARK ASSIST (PAM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">136</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">NO RESPONSE FROM RADIO</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">POSSIBLE CAUSES</strong><small>الأسباب المحتملة</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Possible Causes FUSED B (+) CIRCUIT OPEN OR SHORTED</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">140</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">RADIO</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>TEST FOR AN INTERMITTENT CONDITION</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Check for any TSB(s) related to the condition. If a TSB applies, perform the procedure outlined in the TSB before continuing.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Make sure the battery voltage is between 10.0 and 16.0 volts.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Check the Radio for any active CAN hardware DTCs, perform DTC before proceeding.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read the Radio status.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the scan tool indicate the Radio is active on the bus?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The no response condition is not present at this time. Using the wiring diagram/schematic as a guide, inspect the wiring for chafed, pierced, pinched, and partially broken wires and the wiring harness connectors for broken, bent, pushed out, and corroded terminals.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE (A933) FUSED B(+) CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN OR SHORT CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The test light must illuminate brightly. Compare the brightness to that of a direct connection to the battery.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Radio C1 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Using a 12-volt test light connected to ground, check the (A933) Fused B(+) circuit at the Radio C1 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the open or short in the (A933) Fused B(+) circuit.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (Z911) GROUND CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Using a 12-volt test light connected to 12-volts, check the (Z911) Ground circuits at the Radio C1 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the open in the (Z911) Ground circuit.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (D177) CAN IHS BUS (+) AND (D178) CAN IHS BUS (-) CIRCUITS FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Front CAN IHS Star Connector C3 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (D177) CAN C Bus (+) circuit between the Front CAN IHS Star Connector C3 harness connector and the Radio C1 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (D178) CAN C Bus (-) circuit between the Front CAN IHS Star Connector C3 harness connector and the Radio C1 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance above 3.0 Ohms for both circuits?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the open in the (D177) CAN IHS Bus (+) or (D178) CAN IHS Bus (-) circuit.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Radio in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to RADIO, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">141</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">NO RESPONSE FROM RBSS (RIGHT BLIND SPOT SENSOR)</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">POSSIBLE CAUSES</strong><small>الأسباب المحتملة</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Possible Causes FUSED B (+) CIRCUIT OPEN OR SHORTED</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">145</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">RIGHT BLIND SPOT SENSOR (LBSS)</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>TEST FOR AN INTERMITTENT CONDITION</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          Check for any TSB(s) related to the condition. If a TSB applies, perform the procedure outlined in the TSB before continuing.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          Make sure the battery voltage is between 10.0 and 16.0 volts.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Check the Right Blind Spot Sensor (RBSS) for any active CAN hardware DTCs, perform DTC before proceeding.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read the RBSS status.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the scan tool indicate the RBSS is active on the bus?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The no response condition is not present at this time. Using the wiring diagram/schematic as a guide, inspect the wiring for chafed, pierced, pinched, and partially broken wires and the wiring harness connectors for broken, bent, pushed out, and corroded terminals.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE (F923) FUSED B(+) CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN OR SHORT CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The test light must illuminate brightly. Compare the brightness to that of a direct connection to the battery.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the RBSS harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Using a 12-volt test light connected to ground, check the (F923) Fused B(+) circuit at the RBSS harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the open or short in the (F923) Fused B(+) circuit.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (Z922) GROUND CIRCUIT(S) FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Using a 12-volt test light connected to 12-volts, check the (Z922) Ground circuits at the RBSS harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly for all circuits?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the open in the (Z922) Ground circuit(s).</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (D117) CAN IHS BUS (+) AND (D118) CAN IHS BUS (-) CIRCUITS FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Rear CAN IHS Star Connector C5 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (D117) CAN C Bus (+) circuit between the Rear CAN IHS Star Connector C5 harness connector and the RBSS harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (D118) CAN C Bus (-) circuit between the Rear CAN IHS Star Connector C5 harness connector and the RBSS harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance above 3.0 Ohms for both circuits?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the open in the (D117) CAN IHS Bus (+) or (D118) CAN IHS Bus (-) circuit.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Right Blind Spot Sensor (RBSS) in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Refer to MODULE, BLIND SPOT (BSM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">146</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">NO RESPONSE FROM RFH (RADIO FREQUENCY HUB) MODULE</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">POSSIBLE CAUSES</strong><small>الأسباب المحتملة</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Possible Causes FUSED B(+) CIRCUIT OPEN OR SHORTED</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">149</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">RADIO FREQUENCY HUB (RF HUB) MODULE</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK THE RADIO FREQUENCY HUB STATUS ON THE CAN C BUS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read the Module status.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Does the scan tool indicate that the Module is active on the bus?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension and repair as necessary. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE (A910) FUSED B(+) CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN OR SHORT TO GROUND</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          Leave the scan tool</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">connected</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">and on the initial network screen.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the RF Hub Module C1 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With a 12-volt test light connected to ground, check the (A910) Fused B(+) circuit at the RF Hub Module C1 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The test light must illuminate brightly. Compare the brightness to that of a direct connection to the battery.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (A910) Fused B(+) circuit for an open or short to ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (Z916) GROUND CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN OR HIGH RESISTANCE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With a 12-volt test light connected to 12 volts, check the (Z916) Ground circuit at the RF Hub Module C1 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (Z916) Ground circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE CAN C BUS (+) CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN OR HIGH RESISTANCE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the voltage between ground and the (D40) CAN C Bus (+) circuit at the RF Hub Module C1 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the voltage below 2.5 volts?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (D40) CAN C Bus (+) circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 5</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>CHECK THE CAN C BUS (-) CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN OR HIGH RESISTANCE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the voltage between ground and the (D39) CAN C Bus (-) circuit at the RF Hub Module C1 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the voltage below 1.3 volts?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (D39) CAN C Bus (-) circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the RF Hub Module in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, RADIO FREQUENCY (RF HUB), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">150</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">NO RESPONSE FROM SCCM (STEERING COLUMN CONTROL MODULE)</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">POSSIBLE CAUSES</strong><small>الأسباب المحتملة</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Possible Causes FUSED B(+) CIRCUIT OPEN OR SHORT TO GROUND</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">154</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">STEERING COLUMN CONTROL MODULE (SCCM)</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK THE MODULE STATUS ON THE CAN C BUS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read the CAN topology on the Vehicle View screen.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the Vehicle View screen indicate that the Module is active on the bus?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct terminal tension and repair as necessary. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE (A929) FUSED B(+) CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN OR SHORT TO GROUND</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          The CAN bus will remain active with the scan tool connected and the ignition off.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          Leave the scan tool connected</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">and on the Vehicle View screen.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Steering Column Control Module (SCCM) C1 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The test light must illuminate brightly. Compare the brightness to that of a direct connection to the battery.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With a 12-volt test light connected to ground, check the (A929) Fused B(+) circuit at the SCCM C1 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (A929) Fused B(+) circuit for an open or short to ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (Z911) GROUND CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN OR HIGH RESISTANCE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With a 12-volt test light connected to 12 volts, check the (Z911) Ground circuit at the SCCM C1 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (Z911) Ground circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (D97) CAN C BUS (+) CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN OR HIGH RESISTANCE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the voltage between ground and the (D97) CAN C Bus (+) circuit at the SCCM C1 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the voltage below 2.5 volts?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (D97) CAN C Bus (+) circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 5</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>CHECK THE (D98) CAN C BUS (-) CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN OR HIGH RESISTANCE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the voltage between ground and the (D98) CAN C Bus (-) circuit at the SCCM C1 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the voltage below 1.3 volts?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (D98) CAN C Bus (-) circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Steering Column Control Module (SCCM) in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, STEERING COLUMN CONTROL (SCCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">155</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">NO RESPONSE FROM TCM (TRANSMISSION CONTROL MODULE) - NAG1</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">POSSIBLE CAUSES</strong><small>الأسباب المحتملة</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Possible Causes GROUND CIRCUIT OPEN</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">159</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">TRANSMISSION CONTROL MODULE (TCM)</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Always perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding. Refer to COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>TEST FOR INTERMITTENT CONDITION</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          Check for any TSB(s) related to the condition. If a TSB applies, perform the procedure outlined in the TSB before continuing.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Make sure the battery voltage is between 10.0 and 16.0 volts.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read the module status.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Check the BCM for any active CAN hardware DTCs, perform DTC before proceeding.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Does the scan tool indicate that the module is active on the bus?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The no response condition is not present at this time. Using the wiring diagram/schematic as a guide, inspect the wiring for chafed, pierced, pinched, and partially broken wires and the wiring harness connectors for broken, bent, pushed out, and corroded terminals.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE (Z901) GROUND CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Transmission Control Module C1 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Using a 12-volt test light connected to 12-volts, check the (Z901) ground circuit.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (Z901) ground circuit for an open.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the NAG1 TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to NAG1 TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>(T16) FUSED TRANSMISSION RELAY OUTPUT CIRCUIT OPEN OR SHORTED</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using a 12-volt test light connected to ground, check the (T16) Fused Transmission Relay Output circuit.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (T16) Fused Transmission Relay Output circuit for an open or short.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the NAG1 TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to NAG1 TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (D64) AND (D65) CAN C BUS CIRCUITS FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Front CAN C Star Connector C7 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (D65) CAN C Bus (+) circuit between the Front CAN C Star Connector C7 harness connector and the TCM C1 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (D64) CAN C Bus (-) circuit between the Front CAN C Star Connector C7 harness connector and the TCM C1 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Are the resistances below 5.0 Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Replace and program the Transmission Control Module in accordance with the Service Information. (Refer to MODULE, TRANSMISSION CONTROL, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the NAG1 TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to NAG1 TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair the open in the (D64) or (D65) CAN C Bus circuit.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the NAG1 TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to NAG1 TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">160</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">NO RESPONSE FROM TCM (TRANSMISSION CONTROL MODULE) 8-SPEED</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">POSSIBLE CAUSES</strong><small>الأسباب المحتملة</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Possible Causes FUSED B (+) CIRCUIT OPEN OR SHORTED</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">166</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">TRANSMISSION CONTROL MODULE (TCM)</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Always perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding. Refer to COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK THE MODULE STATUS ON THE CAN C BUS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read the CAN topology on the Vehicle View screen.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the Vehicle View screen indicate that the Module is active on the bus?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct terminal tension and repair as necessary. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. For 8HP45/845ERefer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST . For 8HP70, Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST . For 8HP90, Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST . For NAG1, Refer to NAG1 TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE (A190) FUSED B(+) CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN OR SHORT TO GROUND</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          The CAN bus will remain active with the scan tool connected and the ignition off.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          Leave the scan tool connected</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">and on the Vehicle View screen.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the TCM harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With a 12-volt test light connected to ground, check the (A190) Fused B(+) circuit at the TCM harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The test light must illuminate brightly. Compare the brightness to that of a direct connection to the battery.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (A190) Fused B(+) circuit for an open or short to ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. For 8HP45/845ERefer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST . For 8HP70, Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST . For 8HP90, Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST . For NAG1, Refer to NAG1 TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (F1) IGNITION OFF/RUN/START CONTROL OUTPUT CIRCUIT FOR VOLTAGE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With a 12-volt test light connected to ground, check the (F1) Ignition Off/Run/Start Control Output circuit at the TCM harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 6</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (F1) IGNITION OFF/RUN/START CONTROL OUTPUT CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO GROUND</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the appropriate BCM harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Check for continuity between ground and the (F1) Ignition Off/Run/Start Control Output circuit at the BCM harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between ground and the (F1) Ignition Off/Run/Start Control Output circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (F1) Ignition Off/Run/Start Control Output circuit for a short to ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. For 8HP45/845ERefer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST . For 8HP70, Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST . For 8HP90, Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST . For NAG1, Refer to NAG1 TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 5</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>CHECK THE (F1) IGNITION OFF/RUN/START CONTROL OUTPUT CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (F1) Ignition Off/Run/Start Control Output circuit between the BCM harness connector and the TCM C1 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 3.0 Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the BCM in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, BODY CONTROL (BCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. For 8HP45/845ERefer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST . For 8HP70, Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST . For 8HP90, Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST . For NAG1, Refer to NAG1 TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (F1) Ignition Off/Run/Start Control Output circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. For 8HP45/845ERefer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST . For 8HP70, Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST . For 8HP90, Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST . For NAG1, Refer to NAG1 TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>CHECK THE Z904 GROUND CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN OR HIGH RESISTANCE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With a 12-volt test light connected to 12 volts, check the (Z904) Ground circuit at the TCM harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 7</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (Z904) Ground circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. For 8HP45/845ERefer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST . For 8HP70, Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST . For 8HP90, Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST . For NAG1, Refer to NAG1 TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>CHECK THE (D29) CAN C BUS (+) CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN OR HIGH RESISTANCE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the voltage on the (D29) CAN C Bus (+) circuit at the TCM harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the voltage below 2.5 volts?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (D29) CAN C Bus (+) circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. For 8HP45/845ERefer to</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST . For 8HP70, Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST . For 8HP90, Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST . For NAG1, Refer to NAG1 TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 8</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>CHECK THE (D30) CAN C BUS (-) CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN OR HIGH RESISTANCE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the voltage on the (D30) CAN C Bus (-) circuit at the TCM harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the voltage below 1.3 volts?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (D30) CAN C Bus (-) circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. For 8HP45/845ERefer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST . For 8HP70, Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST . For 8HP90, Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST . For NAG1, Refer to NAG1 TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the TCM in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, TRANSMISSION CONTROL (TCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST. For 8HP45/845ERefer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST . For 8HP70, Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST . For 8HP90, Refer to TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST . For NAG1, Refer to NAG1 TRANSMISSION VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">167</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">NO RESPONSE FROM TPM (TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING) MODULE</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">POSSIBLE CAUSES</strong><small>الأسباب المحتملة</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Possible Causes FUSED B(+) CIRCUIT OPEN OR SHORTED</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">171</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM) MODULE</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>TEST FOR INTERMITTENT CONDITION</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Check for any Service Bulletins related to the condition. If a Service Bulletin applies, perform the procedure outlined in the Service Bulletin before continuing with this procedure.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Make sure the battery voltage is between 10.0 and 16.0 volts.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read the module status.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Check the BCM for any active CAN hardware DTCs, perform DTC before proceeding.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the scan tool indicate that the module is active on the bus?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The no response condition is not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE (A943) FUSED B(+) CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN OR SHORT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the TPM Module harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The test light must illuminate brightly. Compare the brightness to that of a direct connection to the battery.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Using a 12-volt test light connected to ground, check the (A943) Fused B(+) circuit at the TPM harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the open or short in the (A943) Fused B(+) circuit.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TPM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TPM VERIFICATION .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (Z922) GROUND CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Using a 12-volt test light connected to 12-volts, check the (Z922) Ground circuit at the TPM harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the open in the (Z922) Ground circuit.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TPM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TPM VERIFICATION .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (D93) CAN C (+) BUS CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the Star CAN C Rear C4 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (D93) CAN C (+) bus circuit between the Star CAN C Rear C4 harness connector and the TPM Module harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 3.0 Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 5</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the open in the (D93) CAN C (+) bus circuit.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TPM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TPM VERIFICATION .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>CHECK THE (D94) CAN C (-) BUS CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (D94) CAN C (-) bus circuit between the Star CAN C Rear C4 harness connector and the TPM Module harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 3.0 Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Tire Pressure Monitoring (TPM) module in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, TIRE PRESSURE MONITORING (TPM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TPM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TPM VERIFICATION .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the open in the (D94) CAN C (-) bus circuit.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TPM VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to TPM VERIFICATION .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">172</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">STORED LOST COMMUNICATION DTCS</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">For a complete wiring diagram, refer to appropriate SYSTEM WIRING DIAGRAMS article .</p></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">WHEN MONITORED</strong><small>متى يتحقق</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">The ignition is on for greater than five seconds. The battery voltage is between 10.0 and 16.0 volts.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">The Body Control Module (BCM) is configured correctly.</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">SET CONDITION</strong><small>شرط التسجيل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">CAN Bus messages are not received for greater than two seconds.</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">POSSIBLE CAUSES</strong><small>الأسباب المحتملة</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Possible Causes CAN C BUS CIRCUITS OPEN OR SHORT</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">181</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">CHECK FOR RELATED SERVICE BULLETINS</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>VERIFY DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLE CODE (DTC) IS STORED</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Stored faults may indicate a customer perceived intermittent condition.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Make sure the battery voltage is between 10 and 16 volts before proceeding.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read stored DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is this DTC stored?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go to and perform the appropriate diagnostic procedure.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE ENVIRONMENTAL DATA</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read the loss of communication environmental data.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the loss of communication environmental odometer data match up to any of the previous service procedures listed in the possible causes or are there any stored CAN C hardware electrical, battery, ignition voltage, VIN missing/mismatch, or BCM configuration DTCs present with matching environmental data?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">These DTCs may have been the result of other service procedures performed. Clear the DTCs.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>VERIFY INTERMITTENT LOST COMMUNICATION DTC - WIRING CONCERNS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read all DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Is there more than one ECU with stored DTCs &quot;Logged Against&quot; the module and one or more lost communication DTCs stored in the sending module?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Verify if the vehicle was recently in for this type of service. Otherwise, visually inspect the related wiring harness for chafed, pierced, pinched, and partially broken wires and the wiring harness connectors for broken, bent, pushed out, and corroded terminals. Repair as necessary.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>VERIFY INTERMITTENT LOST COMMUNICATION DTC - SENDING MODULE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read all DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Is there more than one ECU with stored DTCs &quot;Logged Against&quot; the module and NO lost communication DTCs stored in the sending module?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Check for a Service Bulletin related to this sending module.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 5</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>VERIFY INTERMITTENT LOST COMMUNICATION DTC - REPORTING MODULE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read all DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Is there ONLY ONE ECU with stored DTCs &quot;Logged Against&quot; the module?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Check for a Service Bulletin related to the module that set this DTC.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Verify if the vehicle was recently in for this type of service. Otherwise, visually inspect the related wiring harness for chafed, pierced, pinched, and partially broken wires and the wiring harness connectors for broken, bent, pushed out, and corroded terminals. Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Article GUID: A00910305</p></div></div></details></div></details>";
